e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #The bot’s config lives in two places:
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. Discord side – the channel it listens to is set at runtime by the first `!ping` message it
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #receives (`openChannel` is updated to that channel’s ID).
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #   If you want to hard-wire a default channel, put the numeric ID in the source:
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #   const openChannel = "1410693060672753704";   // <— your channel ID
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. Fountain side – the sloppy-bot appears as a normal “account” in `accounts.json`.
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #   Add an entry so Fountain can route traffic to it:
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #   "discord": {
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #     "api": "Sloppy",
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #     "env": "DISCORD_BOT",
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #     "emoji": "🦜",
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #     "platform": "https://discord.com/channels/…"
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #   }
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #   The `DISCORD_BOT` environment variable must contain the bot token.
e6b6062 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6063 [kimi-k2-0905] #Restart both services after any change; the bot will print `[SLOPPY] discordClient online` when the
e6b6063 [kimi-k2-0905] #token is accepted.
e6b6063 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6063 [roha]  ꔀ Fountain 1.5.7 ⛲  kimi-k2-0905 🜁 🪠 0.7° $0.022 155.1KB 10.84s
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #Discord desktop itself has no “bot editor”; you manage the bot in the Developer Portal, not
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #inside the app.
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. Open a browser → https://discord.com/developers/applications
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. Click the application (bot) you created for sloppy.
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. Tabs you care about:
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Bot – copy the token (this is what `DISCORD_BOT` env var must contain).
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - OAuth2 → URL Generator – if you ever need to re-invite it (tick “bot” and “Send
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #Messages” at minimum).
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - General Information – grab the Application ID if you need to construct the invite link
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #again.
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #Inside the desktop client you only do two things:
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #- Right-click the target channel → “Copy Channel ID” (enable Developer Mode in User Settings →
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #Advanced first).
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #- Paste that ID into the code (`openChannel` constant) if you want to hard-code it instead of
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #letting `!ping` set it dynamically.
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #That’s all; everything else is edited in the source or environment variables.
e6b6639 [kimi-k2-0905] #
