e6b7c17 [roha]    The bot’s config lives in two places: 1. Discord side – the channel it listens to is set at
e6b7c17 [roha]    runtime by the first `!ping` message it receives (`openChannel` is updated to that channel’s
e6b7c18 [roha]    ID). If you want to hard-wire a default channel, put the numeric ID in the source: ```ts const
e6b7c18 [roha]    openChannel = "1410693060672753704"; // <— your channel ID ``` 2. Fountain side – the
e6b7c18 [roha]    sloppy-bot appears as a normal “account” in `accounts.json`. Add an entry so Fountain can
e6b7c18 [roha]    route traffic to it: ```json "discord": { "api": "Sloppy", "env": "DISCORD_BOT", "emoji":
e6b7c18 [roha]    "🦜", "platform": "https://discord.com/channels/…" } ``` The `DISCORD_BOT` environment
e6b7c18 [roha]    variable must contain the bot token. Restart both services after any change; the bot will
e6b7c18 [roha]    print `[SLOPPY] discordClient online` when the token is
e6b7c18 [roha]    accepted.
