e6b85ea [roha]    Discord desktop itself has no “bot editor”; you manage the bot in the **Developer Portal**,
e6b85ea [roha]    not inside the app. 1. Open a browser → https://discord.com/developers/applications 2. Click
e6b85ea [roha]    the application (bot) you created for sloppy. 3. Tabs you care about: - **Bot** – copy the
e6b85ea [roha]    token (this is what `DISCORD_BOT` env var must contain). - **OAuth2 → URL Generator** – if you
e6b85ea [roha]    ever need to re-invite it (tick “bot” and “Send Messages” at minimum). - **General
e6b85ea [roha]    Information** – grab the Application ID if you need to construct the invite link again. Inside
e6b85ea [roha]    the desktop client you only do two things: - Right-click the target channel → “Copy Channel
e6b85ea [roha]    ID” (enable Developer Mode in User Settings → Advanced first). - Paste that ID into the code
e6b85ea [roha]    (`openChannel` constant) if you want to hard-code it instead of letting `!ping` set it
e6b85ea [roha]    dynamically. That’s all; everything else is edited in the source or environment
e6b85ea [roha]    variables.
