e6db13a [gpt-5-2025] #model uses the v1/responses endpoint. In that case relay() builds payload.messages with
e6db13b [gpt-5-2025] #strictHistory(), which keeps roles and prefixes each message with [source] (e.g. [user], [model],
e6db13b [gpt-5-2025] #etc.), and preserves tool_calls.
e6db13b [gpt-5-2025] #- Otherwise it uses plainHistory() (or multiHistory() for multimodal).
e6db13b [gpt-5-2025] #
e6db13b [gpt-5-2025] #The “Feel free to comment if shared files are new or different.” line is a nudge added after a file
e6db13b [gpt-5-2025] #share/commit changed (“dirty”) so you can add context; safe to ignore if not needed.
