e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #Potential issues and quick fixes
e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #- Startup resilience: wrap startSSHServer in try/catch and provide a clear startup error if host
e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #key is missing.
e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #- Graceful shutdown: ensure server.close() and all sessions end cleanly on SIGINT/exit.
e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #- Typing: many any types (session, stream). Introduce interfaces for SSHSession and fountain
e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #interface to improve type safety.
e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #- Security defaults: consider validating hostKey permissions and restrict where the host key can be
e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #read.
e6e1fc7 [gpt-5-nano] #- Logging verbosity: add a small log level switch so verbose logs aren’t always emitted in
