e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #The files are new to me.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #The codebase is a Deno-based “slop fountain” that lets multiple users chat with multiple LLMs
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #through a single console/SSH/discord bridge.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #Key points:
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #- `slopfountain.ts` is the main orchestrator; it keeps a shared history array (`rohaHistory`) and
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #relays prompts to whichever model is currently active (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, DeepSeek).
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #- `slopprompt.ts` replaces the normal `prompt()` with a raw-mode input loop that also listens on
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #TCP :8081 for remote clients; it returns either a local line or a batch of remote messages.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #- `sloppylisten.ts` is an SSH server (port 6669) that turns each SSH session into a fake “user”
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #whose lines are injected into the same TCP :8081 channel.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #- `sloppybot.ts` is a Discord bot that does the same for Discord messages.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #- All three clients speak NDJSON to the fountain, so from the fountain’s point of view the source
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #is always “somebody sent a line on TCP :8081”.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #The crash you saw (`Windows stdio … non-UTF-8`) happens when the raw console tries to write a byte
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #sequence that is not valid UTF-8.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #The immediate workaround is to start Deno with `--unstable` and pipe stdout/stderr to a file or to
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #`conhost` instead of letting the raw console handle it.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #A proper fix is to sanitise every outgoing chunk with `new TextDecoder("utf-8", {fatal:false})` so
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #broken bytes become � instead of throwing.
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #If you want SSH input to appear in the local `forge.log` exactly like console input, add one line
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #inside `sloppylisten.ts` after the NDJSON is assembled:
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #await logForge(line, name);   // name is the SSH session id
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466e9 [kimi-k2-0905] #(or extend the fountain side so anything received on :8081 is echoed back to the log).
e8466ea [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466ea [kimi-k2-0905] #Let me know if you need a minimal patch or a Windows start-up script.
e8466ea [kimi-k2-0905] #
e8466ea [roha]  ꔀ Fountain 1.5.7 ⛲  kimi-k2-0905 🜁 🪠 0.7° $0.030 203.8KB 34.43s
