e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #Summary after reading the shared tree:
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. No auth gate on Discord → anyone in the channel can drive the bot and therefore the Fountain
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #shell.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #   If that channel is public, random users can run any `/command`, including `/share`, `/push`,
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #`/reset`, or indirectly trigger file-system writes via tool calls.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. Path leakage still exists:
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - `slopfountain.ts` prints absolute Windows paths (`C:\nitrologic\…`) in `/history`, `/share`,
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #and error echoes.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Those lines go straight into `forge.log` and are echoed back to Discord without scrubbing.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. Command injection surface:
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Discord input is forwarded as-is to `callCommand`; no whitelist for Discord-side users.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Tool-call results from the model are re-parsed and can contain back-tick fenced code blocks
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #that Discord will render—no sanitisation before broadcast.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #4. File-system limits are only size-based (`MaxFileSize`); no per-user quota or chroot.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #5. No audit trail that ties Discord message → executed command → side effects; only a shared
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #`forge.log` timestamped in 1/16 s hex.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #Quick hardening you can add right now:
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #- In `sloppybot.ts` drop any line that starts with `/` unless the author ID is in a hard-coded
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #allow-list.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #- In `slopfountain.ts` run every outgoing echo through a cheap redactor:
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #  const safe = line.replace(/[A-Z]:[\/\\][^\s]+/gi, "<local-path>");
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #- Disable dangerous commands from remote users (`/share`, `/push`, `/reset`, `/cd`, `/dir`) unless
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #a `--unsafe` flag is supplied at start-up.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #Beyond that the code is solid; those three changes close the obvious public-channel holes.
e919781 [kimi-k2-0905] #
