e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #Every emoji that is followed by U+FE0F in the source ends up as two code-points, but Discord
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #normalises them away, so the pasted text no longer contains the selector and the fixed-width table
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #cell looks empty.
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #In other words the lines that appear blank are the ones whose original byte sequence was
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #`<emoji> U+FE0F`
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #and after Discord’s normalisation only
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #`<emoji>`
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #remains. Because the width-counting logic still allocates two columns for the original pair, the
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #cell is padded as if the selector were still there, so you see the pipe borders with nothing
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #between them.
e933183 [kimi-k2-0905] #
