f90bfe7 [nitro@ryzen5] i need a trust thing between my nodes
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #Use AWS IAM + Instance Profiles—no keys to rotate, no passwords.
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. One IAM role (e.g. `GameNodeRole`) with the smallest policy you need
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #   {
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #     "Version": "2012-10-17",
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #     "Statement": [{
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #       "Effect": "Allow",
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #       "Action": ["ec2:DescribeInstances", "ec2:DescribeTags"],
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #       "Resource": "*"
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #     }]
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #   }
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. Launch every spot node with that role (console or `--iam-instance-profile Name=GameNodeRole`).
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. Inside the node, fetch temporary creds from
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #   `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/GameNodeRole`
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #   (AWS SDKs do this automatically).
f90c175 [kimi-k2-0905] #
f90c176 [kimi-k2-0905] #4. Node-to-node calls: sign requests with those creds (SigV4) or use the role ARN in a resource
f90c176 [kimi-k2-0905] #policy so each node can verify the caller’s identity.
f90c176 [kimi-k2-0905] #
f90c176 [kimi-k2-0905] #No shared secrets, no certs to renew—IAM handles rotation and revocation.
