f93050f [nitro@ryzen5] when configuring v8 what is v8_enable_i18n_support
f93058f [kimi-k2-0905] #`v8enablei18n_support` is a GN build-time flag that tells V8 whether to build-in the ICU
f93058f [kimi-k2-0905] #library (International Components for Unicode).
f93058f [kimi-k2-0905] #- `true` (default on desktop) – enables the full ECMA-402 Intl object (Intl.DateTimeFormat,
f93058f [kimi-k2-0905] #Intl.NumberFormat, etc.) and makes the resulting `d8` / `libv8` depend on ICU data.
f93058f [kimi-k2-0905] #- `false` – compiles V8 without ICU; the Intl object is not exposed, and the binary has no ICU
f93058f [kimi-k2-0905] #dependency (smaller, but breaks any JS that uses `Intl.*`).
f93058f [kimi-k2-0905] #
