fa43d77 [nitro@ryzen5] what is raspberry pi pico toolchain, bare 32 or 64 bit arm?
fa43dd8 [kimi-k2-0905] #The official Raspberry Pi Pico toolchain targets the RP2040 which contains dual Arm
fa43dd8 [kimi-k2-0905] #Cortex-M0+ cores – these are 32-bit only, so the toolchain is bare-metal 32-bit ARM
fa43dd8 [kimi-k2-0905] #(ARMv6-M).
fa43dd8 [kimi-k2-0905] #
fa43dd8 [roha]  ꔀ Fountain 1.5.7 ⛲  kimi-k2-0905 🜁 🪠 0.7° $0.000 537B 5.22s
fa43f89 [nitro@ryzen5] can i build v8 with depot tools for such a target?
fa44035 [kimi-k2-0905] #No.
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #V8’s build system (gn + ninja) only supports:
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #- 32-bit Arm with VFP (ARMv7-A and newer)
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #- 64-bit Arm (AArch64)
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #Cortex-M0+ is ARMv6-M, no VFP, no MMU, 264 kB on-chip RAM.
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #Even if you hack the toolchain, V8’s baseline interpreter alone is >600 kB and needs an OS for
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #memory mapping and signals. It will not link, let alone run.
fa44036 [kimi-k2-0905] #
fa44036 [roha]  ꔀ Fountain 1.5.7 ⛲  kimi-k2-0905 🜁 🪠 0.7° $0.000 981B 10.06s
fa442f7 [nitro@ryzen5] i am interested in hosting it given these constraints
fa44384 [kimi-k2-0905] #Host it elsewhere.
fa44384 [kimi-k2-0905] #Run a minimal 64-bit Arm (or x86-64) board as the V8 engine and let the Pico talk to it over
fa44384 [kimi-k2-0905] #UART/SPI/I²C.
fa44384 [kimi-k2-0905] #The Pico stays a 32-bit bare-metal device; V8 never lives on it.
fa44385 [kimi-k2-0905] #
fa44385 [roha]  ꔀ Fountain 1.5.7 ⛲  kimi-k2-0905 🜁 🪠 0.7° $0.000 1.570KB 6.15s
fa445c8 [nitro@ryzen5] is there more suitable js engine for embedded?
