10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #The client-side UART sketch you posted is complete enough to exercise the missing server pieces.
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #In the current fit3 tree the only thing that exists is the `sys.ports` stub in `connections.h`;
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #everything else the JS expects (`sys.open`, `sys.write`, `sys.close`, `sys.remove`, plus the
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #`uart.rx` event) is un-implemented.
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #If you want to keep the audio device layer generic, the shortest path is:
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. Finish the server UART support (termios open/close, non-blocking read thread, push `uart.rx`
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #events into the sink).
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. Re-use the same Device base class you already have for ALSA so that an “audio” device and a
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #“com” device are just different subclasses that speak packets and post events.
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. Expose a single `sys.open` that can return either type depending on the path you hand it
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #(`/dev/ttyUSBx` vs `hw:x`).
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #That keeps the JS side unchanged and lets you swap or combine audio and serial devices without
10101e28 [kimi-k2-0905] #extra RPC verbs.
10101e29 [kimi-k2-0905] #
