101021c4 [nitro@ryzen5] no sys.read?
1010224e [kimi-k2-0905] #Correct—there’s no `sys.read` entry in the dispatch table at all.
1010224e [kimi-k2-0905] #The client code you posted never calls it either; it expects inbound data to arrive as unsolicited
1010224e [kimi-k2-0905] #`uart.rx` events that the server pushes to the client inside the normal `sys.tick` poll.
1010224e [kimi-k2-0905] #
1010224e [kimi-k2-0905] #If you want a synchronous “pull” flavour you could add `sys.read(handle, byteCount)` later, but the
