103a9470 [nitro@ryzen5] how does redis.run work pls
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #`redis.run` is just another RPC method the server exposes.
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #The call chain is:
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. HTTP POST `/api` with JSON-RPC body
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #   `{ "method":"redis.run", "params":"SET wiki.banner …" }`
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. `http.h → onRequest()` extracts the body and passes it to
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #   `parseRPC(header, body)`
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. `headless.h → InvokeRPC()` sees method == `"redis.run"` and does:
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #   `stereo->redisrun(command, result, true)`
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #4. `redis.h → Redis::redisrun()` wraps the literal command string and calls:
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #   `RedisContext::run(command, result, quoted=true)`
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #5. `RedisContext::run()` forwards the text to hiredis:
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #   `redisCommand(context, command.c_str())`
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #   (or `redisCommandArgv` if the line contains quotes)
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #6. The reply is formatted back to JSON and returned in the HTTP response.
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #No inspection or rewriting of the command is done; whatever the client puts after `"redis.run"` is
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #sent straight to Redis.
103a9597 [kimi-k2-0905] #
