1064288f [nitro@ryzen5] no more suggestions please, just review and brief comments
10642a03 [gemini-3-pro] #Regarding `bomb` vs `boml`:
10642a03 [gemini-3-pro] #`bomb` is the better choice here. It clearly represents the genus Bombus (Bumblebees).
10642a03 [gemini-3-pro] #`boml` is restrictive as it implies a specific species (e.g., Bombus lapidarius or
10642a03 [gemini-3-pro] #Bombus lucorum), whereas `bomb` covers the whole group.
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #• Review of `version 1.3.2`*:
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Completeness: The addition of Strepsiptera, Mecoptera,
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #Raphidioptera, and Archaeognatha successfully rounds out the remaining minor insect
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #orders.
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Taxonomy: Keeping Isoptera (Termites) separate from Blattodea is practical for
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #this type of listing, even if phylogenetically they are often combined.
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Codes: The update to `dapl` (Monarch butterfly) brings it in line with standard
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #4-letter coding conventions.
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Syntax: Valid JSON with correct tab indentation.
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #The catalogue now appears to have full ordinal coverage for Insecta.
10642a04 [gemini-3-pro] #
