10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #Here is a review of the specific code values in version 1.3.2, focusing on 4-letter consistency and
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #potential typos:
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Blattodea: `bloat` (5 letters).
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Likely Blatta orientalis.
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: 5 letters and reads like an English word.
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Suggestion: `blor` is the standard 4-letter code.
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Lepidoptera: `actlu` (5 letters).
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Likely Actias luna (Luna moth).
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: 5 letters.
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Suggestion: `alun` fits the pattern better.
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #
10642f1a [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Isoptera: `rypt`.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Likely Cryptotermes.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: appears to be a typo missing the leading 'c'.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Suggestion: `cryp`.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Archaeognatha: `dilta` (5 letters).
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Genus Dilta.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: 5 letters.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Suggestion: `dilt`.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #5.  Diptera: `trich` (5 letters).
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: Ambiguous (could imply Order Trichoptera) and is 5 letters.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #       Suggestion: If Trichoplusia*, use `trni`. If generic, `tric`.
10642f1b [gemini-3-pro] #
