1066d724 [nitro@ryzen5] hi gemini given the duplicate list from grok, is it easy to see which codes can be removed ?
1066d928 [gemini-3-pro] #Yes, it is straightforward. The duplicates within Diplopoda (and several other orders) are
1066d928 [gemini-3-pro] #exact redundancies, likely caused by merging a "featured" short-list with a full alphabetical list.
1066d928 [gemini-3-pro] #
1066d928 [gemini-3-pro] #For the Diplopoda specifically, the duplicates (`jsca`, `pave`, `ppro`, `tmar`, `tpol`,
1066d928 [gemini-3-pro] #`tspi`) should be removed to maintain a valid Set.
1066d928 [gemini-3-pro] #
1066d928 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the logic to isolate those redundant codes and the resulting JSON array of codes that can
