10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #A single-supply rail-to-rail op-amp (MCP6001, TLV9061, …) wired as a non-inverting amplifier with a
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #small positive offset is the simplest way:
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #Vcc (3 V3)
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #  │
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #  R1 100 k
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #  │
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #  ├───+ op-amp non-inverting input
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #  │   │
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #video──R2 10 k──┤   gain = 1 + (R3 / R4) ≈ 4
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #  │   │           so 0 V→0.4 V, 0.3 V→1.6 V
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #gnd   R4 33 k   │
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #      │         │
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #      └───R3 100 k─── op-amp output → GPIO
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #Now the 0.3 V blanking level sits well above the Pico’s 0.8 V high threshold, so you can treat the
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #op-amp output as a digital blanking flag with no extra parts.
10781134 [kimi-k2-0905] #
