107ac0b3 [gemini-3-pro] #• Bandwidth Analysis*
107ac0b3 [gemini-3-pro] #• Throughput: 3,840,000 pixels/sec × 2 bits = 7.68 Mbps (0.96 MB/s).
107ac0b3 [gemini-3-pro] #• USB 1.1 Limit: The RP2040 USB hardware is Full Speed (12 Mbps).
107ac0b3 [gemini-3-pro] #• Feasibility: Your required throughput consumes roughly 64% of the raw bus bandwidth. Once
107ac0b4 [gemini-3-pro] #you account for USB protocol overhead (packet headers, CRCs, bit-stuffing), this is feasible but
107ac0b4 [gemini-3-pro] #tight. You will likely need to use double-buffered Bulk or Isochronous transfers with DMA to
107ac0b4 [gemini-3-pro] #maintain this rate without dropped frames.
107ac0b4 [gemini-3-pro] #
107ac0b4 [gemini-3-pro] #• Hardware Design*
107ac0b4 [gemini-3-pro] #• LM319: With a response time of ~80ns, these comparators are fast enough for the pixel
