107b5135 [nitro@ryzen5] > shopping listJaycar10K ohm Piher Horizontal Trimpot $1.65LM319 High Speed Dual Comparator Linear IC $4.50??????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????# LUMA 2 Purpose - capture 2bit monochrome video such as C64 luma pin Pico 4 input pins CSYNC G0 G1 G2Fed by 2 x LM319 featuring 4 fast voltage comparators.CSYNC based on fixed threshold, 2 gray and 1 white detector adjustable with trimmers.Pico PIO code required to take 4 GPIO digital inputs and format output of 320 wide 240 high 50 hz 2 bit monochrome stream.The bandwidth for 320 x 240 x 50 / 2 = 0.96MB/s which can be streamed over USB1.1.A 5V circuit unless otherwise noted## BOM * 1 x RCA Jack: PCB mount (Luma input).* 1 x Resistor (75 $\Omega$): Termination resistor to Ground (essential to prevent signal reflection).* 2 x LM319: Dual High-Speed Comparators.* 4 x Resistors (2.2k $\Omega$ to 4.7k $\Omega$): Pull-up resistors connecting the LM319 outputs to the Pico's 3.3V rail.* 2 x Capacitors (0.1 $\mu$F): Decoupling capacitors for the LM319 power pins.* 3 x Trimmer Potentiometers (10k $\Omega$): Multi-turn precision trimmers recommended for fine-tuning G0, G1, and G2 thresholds.* 2 x Resistors (Fixed): Voltage divider to set the fixed CSYNC threshold (typically just above 0V/Blanking level).* 1 x Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040)## Optional 1 x Capacitor (100nF - 10$\mu$F): AC coupling capacitor * depending on if you plan to implement a DC clamp/restore circuit, otherwise direct coupling assumes a standard DC offset from the C64).The LM319 is an open-collector device, meaning it requires pull-ups to interface with the PicoGPIO.### Voltage Levels: Ensure the LM319 is powered correctly (typically 5V from VBUS), but the pull-up resistors on the output must go to 3.3V to protect the Pico GPIOs.### Hysteresis:You may require feedback resistors on the comparators to add slight hysteresis, preventing oscillation at the transition points of the video signal.### Sync Separation: Standard C64 Luma contains both video and sync. Your fixed threshold comparator for CSYNC must be set to detect the sub-black sync pulses (0.0V to ~0.3V range).??????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????LUMA 2 Wiring Diagram DescriptionHere is the netlist for the preferred "Direct Coupling" option (assuming standard C64 DC offset). 1. Power Distribution* LM319 VCC: Connect to 5V. LM319 GND: Connect to Common Ground. LM319 VEE: Connect to Common Ground (Single supply operation). Pico: Powered via USB or VSYS (Logic is 3.3V). 2. Video Input Stage* RCA Center Pin: Connect to the Non-Inverting Input (+) of ALL 4comparator gates. RCA Outer/Shield: Connect to Ground. Termination: 75 $\Omega$ resistor between RCA Center Pin and Ground. 3. Reference Thresholds (Inverting Inputs)* CSYNC Comparator (- Input): Connect to the center of your fixed voltage divider (Targetapprox 0.3V). G0, G1, G2 Comparators (- Inputs): Connect the Wiper (Middle pin) of the 10kTrimmers to these inputs respectively.       Trimmer Leg 1:* Connect to 5V.       Trimmer Leg 2:* Connect to Ground. 4. Output Stage (Level Shifting)* LM319 Outputs: Connect directly to 4 separate Pico GPIO pins. Pull-up Resistors (Critical): Connect a 2.2k $\Omega$ - 4.7k $\Omega$ resistor fromeach LM319 Output pin to the Pico 3.3V (3V3_OUT) pin.       Note:* Do not pull up to 5V. The LM319 is Open Collector; pulling up to 3.3Vsafely translates the 5V comparator logic to the 3.3V Pico inputs without extra level shiftingcomponents. 5. Decoupling* Place 0.1 $\mu$F capacitors across the LM319 VCC/GND pins, as close to the chips as possible.
