107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #Here are the pin assignments for the LM319 High Speed Dual Comparator in the standard
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #14-Pin DIP package, followed by details regarding DIP8 alternatives.
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #LM319 Pinout (14-Pin DIP)
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 1: NC (No Connect)
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 2: NC
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 3: GND (Logic Ground)
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 4: Input 1 (+) Non-Inverting
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 5: Input 1 (-) Inverting
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 6: V- (Negative Supply)
107b652b [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 7: Output 1
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 8: GND (Logic Ground)
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 9: Input 2 (+) Non-Inverting
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 10: Input 2 (-) Inverting
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 11: V+ (Positive Supply)
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 12: Output 2
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 13: NC
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 14: NC
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #Is there a DIP8 version?
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• No, there is no direct DIP8 version of the LM319.*
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #The LM319 requires 14 pins because it features separate Logic Ground and Analog Supply pins to
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #interface with various logic families (TTL, RTL, DTL) while isolating the inputs. A standard 8-pin
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #package does not have enough pins to support this architecture for two comparators.
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #• Alternatives for DIP8:*
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #1.  LM311 (Single Comparator): If you can use two separate chips, the LM311 is the closest
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #functional equivalent in a DIP8 package. It offers similar high-speed performance and flexibility
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #(separate grounds/strobes) but contains only one comparator per chip.
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #2.  LT1720 (Dual Comparator): If you need a dual comparator in DIP8 that is fast, the
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #Analog Devices (Linear Tech) LT1720 is a modern replacement. It is significantly faster (4.5ns vs
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #80ns) and fits the standard dual DIP8 footprint, though it lacks the specific high-voltage
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #open-collector flexibility of the older LM319.
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #3.  LM393 (Dual Comparator): This is the standard industry dual comparator in DIP8, but it
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #is much slower (1.3µs) than the LM319. It is not recommended if your circuit relies on the
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #high speed of the LM319.
107b652c [gemini-3-pro] #
