107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #Regarding the LM319 replacement:
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #The LM319 comes in a 14-pin package because it isolates the input and output
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #grounds/supplies to achieve its high speed (80ns response time).
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #Finding a Dual High-Speed comparator in DIP-8 with equivalent performance is
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #difficult, especially at hobbyist retailers like Jaycar.
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #• LM393 (DIP-8): This is the standard dual comparator, but it is too slow (~1300ns) for C64
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #video signals.
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #• LM311 (DIP-8): This offers comparable speed (~165ns), but it is a single
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #comparator. You would need four chips instead of two LM319s.
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #• TLC372 (DIP-8): Faster than the LM393 (~200ns) but likely still too slow for crisp video
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #edges compared to the LM319.
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #
107b73ad [gemini-3-pro] #• Recommendation:*
107b73ae [gemini-3-pro] #Stick with the LM319. The extra PCB footprint is necessary for the bandwidth required to
107b73ae [gemini-3-pro] #capture the C64 pixel clock cleanly.
107b73ae [gemini-3-pro] #
