107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the reorganized development documentation for the LUMA 2 project.
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #LUMA 2 Project Specification
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #• Purpose:* Capture 2-bit monochrome video (specifically Commodore 64 Luma signal) using a
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #Raspberry Pi Pico.
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #System Overview
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #• Hardware: Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040) + 2x LM319 Dual High-Speed Comparators.
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #• Input Logic: 4 GPIO inputs representing CSYNC, G0 (Gray 1), G1 (Gray 2), and G2 (White).
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #• Software Goal: PIO state machine to format inputs into a 320x240 @ 50Hz 2-bit monochrome
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #stream.
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #• Bandwidth: ~0.96 MB/s (Compatible with USB 1.1 streaming).
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #• Voltage Domain: 5V Analog / 3.3V Digital Logic.
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9c [gemini-3-pro] #Bill of Materials (BOM)
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Semiconductors*
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 1x Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 2x LM319 High-Speed Dual Comparators (e.g., Linear IC).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Passive Components*
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 1x Resistor 75 $\Omega$ (Video Termination).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 4x Resistors 2.2k $\Omega$ – 4.7k $\Omega$ (Logic Pull-ups).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 2x Resistors (Fixed value for CSYNC voltage divider).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 3x Trimmer Potentiometers 10k $\Omega$ (Recommended: Piher Horizontal for G0, G1, G2).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 2x Capacitors 0.1 $\mu$F (Decoupling).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 1x Capacitor 100nF – 10$\mu$F (Optional: AC Coupling if DC clamp is implemented).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Connectors*
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 1x RCA Jack (PCB Mount).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #Wiring & Netlist
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 1. Power Distribution*
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• LM319 VCC: Connect to 5V (VBUS).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• LM319 GND/VEE: Connect to Common Ground (Single supply).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Pico: Powered via USB or VSYS; Logic operates at 3.3V.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Decoupling: Place 0.1 $\mu$F capacitors across LM319 VCC/GND pins close to the ICs.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 2. Video Input Stage*
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Signal: RCA Center Pin connected to the Non-Inverting Input (+) of all 4
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #comparator gates.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Ground: RCA Shield connected to Common Ground.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Termination: 75 $\Omega$ resistor between RCA Center Pin and Ground.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 3. Reference Thresholds (Inverting Inputs)*
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• CSYNC Comparator (- Input): Connect to fixed voltage divider (Target: ~0.3V for sub-black
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #sync pulses).
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• G0, G1, G2 Comparators (- Inputs): Connect to the wiper of individual 10k Trimmers.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #       Trimmer Legs:* Connect Leg 1 to 5V and Leg 2 to Ground.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• 4. Output Stage (Level Shifting)*
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Configuration: Open-Collector outputs.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Signal Path: Connect LM319 Outputs directly to 4 separate Pico GPIO pins.
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #• Pull-ups (Critical): Connect a 2.2k $\Omega$ – 4.7k $\Omega$ resistor from each LM319
107cba9d [gemini-3-pro] #Output pin to Pico 3.3V (3V3_OUT).
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #       Warning:* Do not pull up to 5V. Pulling to 3.3V safely translates the 5V comparator
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #logic to RP2040 voltage tolerance.
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #Design Notes
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Sync Separation: The fixed threshold comparator must detect sub-black sync pulses (0.0V
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #to ~0.3V).
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Hysteresis: Feedback resistors may be required on comparators to prevent oscillation at
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #video transition points.
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #3.  DC Coupling: The current design assumes a standard DC offset from the C64. If AC
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #coupling is added later, a DC clamp/restore circuit is required.
107cba9e [gemini-3-pro] #
