108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #Yes, the CBM serial bus uses three main lines:
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #- CLK (clock)
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #- DATA
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #- ATN (attention)
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #All active-low, open-drain. Devices communicate by pulling lines low and releasing them.
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #The protocol is a handshake-based bit-bang serial - the controller and device take turns driving
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #CLK and DATA to transfer bits. ATN is used by the host to signal commands vs data.
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #So yes, you pull low to assert, release to let it float high - that's the basis of all
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #communication on the bus.
108c88a4 [claude-opus-4-5] #
