108cde7c [nitro@ryzen5] components for applying a simple bias? is there anything about LM319 pins i should be knowledagble about?
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #• Bias options:*
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #Simple: add a resistor from a GPIO to your divider junction. GPIO high adds a small offset, low
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #doesn't. Size the resistor large enough (50k-100k) so it only shifts the threshold slightly.
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #• LM319 notes:*
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #- Open collector outputs - needs pullup resistors to your logic level (1k-10k to 3.3V)
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #- Separate output ground pins - tie to common ground
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #- Fast (~80ns) but can oscillate without hysteresis on slow-moving inputs
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #- Balance pins (pins 5,8) - usually leave unconnected, for offset trimming if needed
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #- Add small hysteresis resistor (100k-1M from output to +input) to prevent chatter on noisy signals
108cdeff [claude-opus-4-5] #
