108d2e83 [nitro@ryzen5] descirbe the clock φ
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #• φ2 (Phi 2):*
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #- ~1 MHz system clock (985 kHz PAL, 1.023 MHz NTSC)
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #- High phase = CPU accesses bus
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #- Low phase = VIC-II accesses bus
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #• Timing:*
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #- Address valid on rising edge
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #- Data read/write during high phase
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #- ~500ns high, ~500ns low
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #• Usage:*
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d2ee7 [claude-opus-4-5] #- Synchronise your cartridge reads/writes to φ2 high
