108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #The 74LVC245 is your best pick. It's 5V tolerant on inputs while running at 3.3V, so it
108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #handles the level shifting naturally.
108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #Get 2-3 of them:
108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #- One for address bus (directly from C64)
108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #- One for data bus (directly from C64)
108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #- One for control signals
108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d4d99 [claude-opus-4-5] #The HC and LS variants won't work properly - they're not 5V tolerant when powered at 3.3V, and
108d4d9a [claude-opus-4-5] #powering them at 5V means their outputs are too high for the RP2040.
108d4d9a [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d4d9a [claude-opus-4-5] #The 74HC374 is useful too - latched outputs could help with address decoding or output
108d4d9a [claude-opus-4-5] #registers if you need them later, but it has the same voltage level issues.
108d4d9a [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d4d9a [claude-opus-4-5] #So: grab the 74LVC245s, skip the others for the interface itself.
108d4d9a [claude-opus-4-5] #
