108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #The 74HC series specifies minimum input high voltage (VIH) as 70% of VCC.
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #At 5V that's 3.5V minimum to guarantee a logic high.
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #The RP2040 outputs 3.3V, so you're 0.2V short of the spec.
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #In practice it'll probably work fine - the actual switching threshold is around 2.5V and most chips
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #will read 3.3V as high. But it's not guaranteed across all temperatures and manufacturing
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #variations.
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #The 74LVC245 at 5V has VIH spec of 2V, so 3.3V is comfortably within spec.
108d535d [claude-opus-4-5] #
