1092ff49 [nitro@ryzen5] # Project LUMA2 Purpose - capture 2bit monochrome video such as C64 luma pin Pico 4 input pins CSYNC G0 G1 G2 Fed by 2 x LM319 featuring 4 fast voltage comparators.CSYNC based on fixed threshold, 2 gray and 1 white detector adjustable with trimmers.Pico PIO code required to take 4 GPIO digital inputs.RP2040 then formats output frames of 320 wide 200 high 50 hz 2 bit monochrome
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #Interesting project! Capturing C64 luma with PIO is a solid approach.
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #• Key challenges I see:*
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #1. Sync detection - CSYNC gives you composite sync, so you'll need to differentiate HSYNC
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #vs VSYNC (typically by pulse width - VSYNC is longer). PIO can measure pulse widths with a counter.
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #2. Pixel clock recovery - C64 doesn't give you a dot clock, so you're sampling
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #asynchronously. At 320 pixels across ~52µs active line, that's ~6.15MHz pixel rate. PIO can
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #oversample and you'd decimate in software, or you tune the PIO clock to approximate the dot rate.
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #3. Gray level encoding - Your 3 comparators give you thermometer code
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #(none/G0/G0+G1/G0+G1+G2 triggered). PIO can read all 4 pins in one instruction and pack them.
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #4. Buffer management - 320×200×2bit = 16KB per frame. At 50Hz you need double buffering and
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #DMA to keep up without CPU intervention during capture.
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #• Questions that would shape the PIO design:*
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #- Are you aiming for free-running capture or genlocked to the C64's timing?
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #- How precise does horizontal positioning need to be, or is some drift acceptable?
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #- Is the LM319 output active-high or active-low into the Pico?
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #The PIO state machine count matters too - one for sync detection, one for pixel capture, or
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #combined?
1093000b [claude-opus-4-5] #
