10933fd4 [nitro@ryzen5] could you make educated guess based on what is known about c64 palette and the luma pin
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #C64 has 16 colors but only 9 distinct luma levels on the luma pin. Roughly:
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #- Black: ~0V
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #- Dark grays: ~0.2-0.3V
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #- Mid grays: ~0.4-0.5V
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #- Light grays: ~0.6-0.7V
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #- White: ~0.8-1.0V
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #With 3 thresholds you're dividing into 4 bands. Optimal placement probably around 0.25V, 0.45V,
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #0.65V to split the range evenly.
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #• For the bias shift:* You want to catch the levels that fall between your main thresholds.
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #The luma steps are roughly 0.1V apart in the mid range.
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #• So a bias of ~50mV* would shift your thresholds to interleave with the base positions.
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #If your trimpot wiper is around 0.45V and you add a 100K resistor to a 3.3V GPIO:
1093407b [claude-opus-4-5] #
