10938cf1 [nitro@ryzen5] # Project LUMA2 Purpose - capture 2bit monochrome video such as C64 luma pin Pico 4 input pins CSYNC G0 G1 G2 Fed by 2 x LM319 featuring 4 fast voltage comparators.CSYNC based on fixed threshold, 2 gray and 1 white detector adjustable with trimmers.Pico PIO code required to take 4 GPIO digital inputs.RP2040 then formats output frames of 320 wide 200 high 50 hz 2 bit monochrome.- 2x LM319 (4 comparators total) ($4.50)- 3x 10K Piher horizontal trimpot ($1.65)- 1x 10K resistor (sync divider)- 1x 1K resistor (sync divider)- 4x 4.7K resistor (pull-ups)- 3x 220K resistor (threshold bias)- 1x 100nF ceramic cap (decoupling)- 1x 75R resistor (video termination)- 1x RCA phono jack PCB mount through-hole# netlist* LM319 VCC: Connect to 5V.* LM319 GND: Connect to Common Ground.* LM319 VEE: Connect to Common Ground (Single supply operation).* RCA Center Pin: Connect to the Non-Inverting Input (+) of ALL 4 comparator gates.* RCA Outer/Shield: Connect to Ground.* Termination: between RCA Center Pin and Ground.* CSYNC Comparator Connect 3V3 rail with voltage divider 10K + 1K to inverting input* G0, G1, G2 Comparator - wiper middle pin to comparator inverting input, leg 1 5v leg 2 ground* LM319 Outputs: Connect directly to 4 separate Pico GPIO pins with internal pullups.* Place capacitors across the LM319 VCC/GND pins, as close to the chips as possible.* Bias resistors: Single GPIO through 220K to each trimpot wiper (G0, G1, G2)* 75R termination: RCA center pin to ground* Optional 4.7K pull-ups: LM319 outputs to 3.3V (one per output) instead of internal pullups
