1097385f [nitro@ryzen5] just to be clear the pio can write a byte of data to GP2..GP9?
109738c6 [claude-opus-4-5] #Yes, PIO can write to any consecutive GPIO pins. GP2-GP9 is 8 consecutive pins, so a single `out
109738c6 [claude-opus-4-5] #pins, 8` instruction with the pin base set to GP2 will do it.
109738c6 [claude-opus-4-5] #
109738c6 [claude-opus-4-5] #Same for reading - `in pins, 8` with base GP2 pulls all 8 bits in one cycle.
109738c6 [claude-opus-4-5] #
109738c6 [claude-opus-4-5] #The PIO pin mapping is flexible as long as they're consecutive for multi-bit operations.
109738c6 [claude-opus-4-5] #
