109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #Hello. I have reviewed the documentation for Project Toast. It looks like a capable interface
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #design for the C64 cartridge port.
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #Here are a few observations regarding the electrical design and consistency:
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #1.  74LVC245 Power Rail: The netlist shows the transceiver V_CC connected to +5V.
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Risk: At 5V, the 74LVC245 typically requires a VIH (Input High) of \approx 3.5V
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #(0.7 × VCC). The RP2040's 3.3V GPIO output may not reliably trigger a high state.
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Suggestion: Power the 74LVC245 at 3.3V. It is 5V tolerant on the C64 side
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #and will drive valid TTL logic levels (~3.3V) to the bus.
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #2.  RP2040 Input Protection: The 74HC165 shift registers are powered at +5V.
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Risk: The `Q7` output lines (GP17–GP20) will drive 5V into the RP2040. The RP2040
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #is not 5V tolerant. While the 10kΩ series resistors will limit the current into the internal
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #clamping diodes, this relies on out-of-spec behavior.
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Documentation Discrepancy:
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The ASCII block diagram lists 3× 74HC165.
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The BOM and Netlist detail 4× 74HC165 (covering Address, Data, and Control lines).
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #Let me know if you need any specific PIO code generation for the shift register timing.
109f20de [gemini-3-pro] #
