109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #Hi. I have reviewed the netlist and BOM for Project Toast.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #It is a split-bus architecture (Input via Shift Registers, Output via Transceiver). While the
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #concept is sound for a ROM emulator or bus sniffer, there is some "slop" in the netlist regarding
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #Pin Conflicts and Voltage Levels that will prevent it from working or potentially damage the
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #RP2040.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #⚠️ The "Slop" Report (Critical Issues)
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• 1. Voltage Logic Levels (The 5V vs 3.3V Issue)*
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• The Issue: Your netlist powers the 74HC165s at +5V (pins 1.16, 2.16,
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #etc). This means the `Q7` outputs (GP17, GP18, GP19, GP20) will drive 5V into the RP2040.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• The Risk: RP2040 GPIOs are not 5V tolerant.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Mitigation: You mentioned "10kΩ series resistors" in the header. If these resistors are
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #placed between the HC165 Q7 pins and the RP2040, you are relying on the RP2040's internal clamping
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #diodes to sink the excess voltage. This is out of spec, but often works in "hacky" scenarios.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Better Fix: Power the 74HC165s at 3.3V. The 74HC series at 3.3V has a V_IH (Input
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #High) of ~2.3V. The C64 (5V TTL/NMOS) outputs will easily trigger this. This makes the Q7 output
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #safe 3.3V logic for the Pico without relying on clamp diodes.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• 2. Pin Conflict: GP10 (/IRQ vs DOT)*
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Allocation List: Lists `GP10, /IRQ active low`.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Direct Inputs: Lists `DOT, GP10`.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Shift Reg 4: Lists `P0, /IRQ` (Input to shift reg).
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Conflict: You cannot drive the Open Drain `/IRQ` line low while simultaneously trying to
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #read the high-speed `DOT` clock (8MHz) on the same pin.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Fix: Move `DOT` clock to a free pin or drop it (DOT clock is rarely needed for standard
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #cart emulation; PHI2 is usually sufficient).
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• 3. Pin Conflict: GP22 (/OE vs R/W)*
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Allocation List: Lists `GP22, R/W edge`.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• 74LVC245 List: Lists `5.19, /OE, GP22`.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Conflict: You are using GP22 to detect the R/W transition and to Enable the Data Bus
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #transceiver.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Logic Failure: If R/W is High (Read), you might want /OE Low (Active) to drive data. If
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #you tie them together, the logic might be inverted or timing will be wrong. These need separate
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #pins.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• 4. 74LVC245 Direction*
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Netlist: `5.1, DIR, 3V3`.
109f291d [gemini-3-pro] #• Effect: Direction is permanently locked A->B (RP2040 -> C64).
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #• Observation: This is correct for a cartridge emulator (RP2040 writes data to C64 during
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #Read cycles). Just ensure your code never enables `/OE` (GP22) when the C64 is writing (R/W
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #Low), or you will cause a bus fight and short circuit.
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #RP2040 PIO Implementation
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #To make this work, you need to read the 4 shift registers in parallel extremely fast to catch the
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #bus state within the PHI2 window. Here is a PIO program to read 32 bits (Address + Data + Control)
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #in just a few cycles.
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #• Wiring Assumption for Code:*
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #• `SIDE_SET` pin: GP15 (CLK)
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #• `SET` pin: GP16 (SH/LD)
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #• `IN` pins base: GP17 (The four Q7 outputs: GP17, 18, 19, 20 mapped to IN 0, 1, 2, 3)
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #// toast.pio
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #.program toast_read
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #.side_set 1
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #// C64 Cycle: ~1us.
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #// We need to latch, shift 8 times, and push to FIFO.
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #// 74HC165: Low on SH/LD loads data. High shifts.
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #// Data is valid on Q7 immediately after Load.
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #public entry_point:
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    set pins, 0     side 0  ; [1] Drive SH/LD Low (Load), CLK Low
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    set pins, 1     side 0  ; [2] Drive SH/LD High (Shift mode)
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    in pins, 4      side 1  ; [3] Sample bit 0 (MSB), Clock High
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    in pins, 4      side 0  ; [4] Sample bit 1, Clock Low
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    in pins, 4      side 1  ; [5] ...
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    in pins, 4      side 0
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    in pins, 4      side 1
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    in pins, 4      side 0
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    in pins, 4      side 1
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    in pins, 4      side 0  ; [10] Sample bit 7
109f291e [gemini-3-pro] #    push block      side 0  ; [11] Push 32 bits to RX FIFO
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #• C SDK Configuration:*
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] ##include "hardware/pio.h"
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] ##include "toast.pio.h"
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #// GPIO Mapping based on your netlist
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] ##define GPIO_CLK    15
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] ##define GPIO_SHLD   16
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] ##define GPIO_Q7_BASE 17 // Expects 17, 18, 19, 20 to be consecutive
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #void toast_init(PIO pio, uint sm) {
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #    uint offset = pio_add_program(pio, &toast_read_program);
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #    pio_sm_config c = toast_read_program_get_default_config(offset);
109f291f [gemini-3-pro] #
