109f6266 [nitro@ryzen5] can dma write to single address multiple times like a CIA?
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Yes, absolutely. DMA can perform multiple writes to the same address, which is exactly how CIA
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #registers and VIC-II registers work.
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### DMA Write Patterns
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Single Address Multiple Writes (CIA/VIC style)
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Common pattern: Writing to I/O registers that trigger actions rather than store data
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Examples:
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- VIC-II sprite coordinates (sequential writes to $D000-$D00F)
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- CIA timer latches (write low byte, write high byte to same register pair)
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- SID voice registers (updating waveform/frequency in rapid succession)
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### DMA Timing Requirements
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Each write cycle requires:
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Setup address on bus
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Assert R/W LOW
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Setup data on bus
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Wait for PHI2 HIGH phase (~500ns)
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Hold data stable
109f6354 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Wait for PHI2 LOW
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Can change address/data for next cycle
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Streaming Pattern Example
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Writing to VIC-II $D012 (raster compare) repeatedly:
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Cycle 1: A=$D012, D=$00, R/W=LOW
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Cycle 2: A=$D012, D=$01, R/W=LOW
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Cycle 3: A=$D012, D=$02, R/W=LOW
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #(Address constant, data changes, R/W stays LOW)
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Implementation Note
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #GP22 (R/W) must remain LOW throughout consecutive write cycles
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #No need to toggle High-Z between writes to same address
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Only address and data lines change between cycles
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #This is useful for effects like raster bars, sprite multiplexing, or audio streaming where you're
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #hammering the same register repeatedly with different values. Is this the use case you're
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #targeting?
109f6355 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
