109f661e [nitro@ryzen5] audio streaming?
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Yes, audio streaming via DMA writes to SID registers or other audio hardware.
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### Audio Streaming via DMA
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### SID Register Updates
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #The SID chip (6581/8580) has registers that can be updated in real-time:
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- $D400-$D418: Voice 1-3 frequency, waveform, ADSR, filter
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Typical pattern: Update voice frequency registers every frame or multiple times per frame
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Example: PCM playback by rapidly updating volume register ($D418)
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### PCM Playback Techniques
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #**Volume Register Method:**
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Write 4-bit samples to $D418 bits 0-3 at ~8kHz-16kHz
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- DMA writes: A=$D418, D=$0x (where x = sample value 0-15)
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Requires precise timing: one write every ~60-120 CPU cycles
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Creates crude but recognizable audio
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #**Waveform Switching Method:**
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Rapidly switch between waveforms and frequencies
109f6721 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Multiple register writes per sample period
109f6722 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Better quality than volume method but more CPU/DMA intensive
109f6722 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6722 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Timing Constraints
109f6722 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #At 1MHz (985kHz actual), maximum theoretical write rate:
109f6722 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- One write per cycle = 985k writes/sec
109f6722 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Practical: ~500k writes/sec (accounting for PHI2 phases)
109f6722 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- For 8kHz audio: 8000 samples/sec = 123 cycles per sample (feasible)
