109f6d7b [nitro@ryzen5] 4 bit at 12khz would be ok for basic speech?
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Yes, 4-bit at 12kHz is adequate for intelligible speech, though quality will be "telephone-like."
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### 4-bit 12kHz Speech Quality
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Audio Characteristics
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Sample rate: 12kHz (Nyquist frequency 6kHz, covers fundamental speech range)
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Bit depth: 4-bit (16 amplitude levels)
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Quality: Comparable to early digital answering machines or CVSD codec
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Intelligibility: Good for speech, poor for music
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Timing Budget (12kHz)
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Samples per second: 12,000
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- C64 cycles per sample: 985,000 / 12,000 ≈ 82 cycles
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- PHI2 periods per sample: ~82 (plenty of headroom)
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- DMA write pattern: A=$D418, D=(sample & 0x0F), R/W=LOW
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Sample Preparation (RP2040 side)
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Source: 8-bit or 16-bit PCM audio
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Downsample to 12kHz
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Reduce to 4-bit (simple: right-shift 4 bits, or use proper dithering)
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Optional: Pre-emphasis filter to improve clarity
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Store in circular buffer
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### DMA Streaming Loop
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #1. Wait for PHI2 rising edge (GP28)
109f6e73 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #2. Load next 4-bit sample from buffer
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #3. Assert DMA if not already bus master
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #4. Write to $D418: (sample & 0x0F) | $x0 (preserve filter bits if needed)
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #5. Advance buffer pointer
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #6. Repeat every 82 cycles
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Quality Improvements
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Companding (µ-law or A-law) before 4-bit conversion improves dynamic range
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Low-pass filter at 6kHz before downsampling prevents aliasing
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- DC offset removal prevents clicks
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #This would work well for simple voice prompts, game speech, or even crude music playback. Are you
109f6e74 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #planning to stream from USB or play back pre-stored samples?
