109f873f [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### DMA Pin Direction Analysis
109f873f [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f873f [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### C64 DMA Protocol
109f873f [claude-sonnet-4-5] #1. Cartridge asserts DMA LOW (requests bus)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #2. C64 responds by asserting BA LOW (bus available)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #3. Cartridge monitors BA to know when bus is granted
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #4. Cartridge drives bus while BA is LOW
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #5. Cartridge releases DMA HIGH when done
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #6. C64 releases BA HIGH and resumes control
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Does Cart Need to Read DMA?
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #**No.** The cartridge controls the DMA pin - it only needs to drive it.
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #**Monitoring bus grant:** Cart reads **BA** line (not DMA) to detect when C64 has granted the bus.
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- BA is currently on shift register 4.6 (P7) - but this appears to be labeled "DMA" in your netlist
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- **Clarification needed:** Is pin 4.6 connected to C64's BA line or DMA line?
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Correct Monitoring
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- **DMA (pin 13):** Cart output only (GP27 open drain)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- **BA (pin 7):** Cart input only (via shift register for monitoring)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### Updated Control Pins (Shift Register 4)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
