109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #4.4, P5, /EXROM   (input)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #4.5, P6, /GAME    (input)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #4.6, P7, BA       (input - monitors bus available)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### GP27 Usage
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #**Output only:** Open drain to DMA line
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Drive LOW to request bus
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Float HIGH (High-Z) when not requesting
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- Never needs to read this pin
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #### BA Monitoring
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #Read BA state from shift register bit (4.6)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- BA HIGH: C64 owns bus
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #- BA LOW: Bus granted to cartridge (can drive address/data if implemented)
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #
109f8740 [claude-sonnet-4-5] #So DMA is output-only, and you monitor BA (not DMA) to detect the grant. Does your netlist pin 4.6
