109fbeaa [nitro@ryzen5] hi gemini, latest version of project toast plan attached
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #Thanks for sharing the latest spec. The parallel shift register readout (4 bits wide × 8 clocks) is
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #a solid architectural choice for keeping up with the ~1MHz PHI2 bus, but there are some electrical
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #risks in the "Slop" approach that might turn "Project Toast" into literal toast.
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #Here is a review of the netlist and logic:
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #1. The "Toast" Risk: Open Drain Signals
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #You correctly identified that Open Drain signals (IRQ, NMI, etc.) should toggle between Low and
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #High-Z. However:
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #• The Problem: C64 control lines are pulled up to 5V. When the RP2040 is in High-Z,
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #the pin is exposed to 5V. The RP2040 is not 5V tolerant (Max V_GPIO is VDDIO + 0.5V).
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #• The 10k Resistor Fix: While a 10k series resistor limits the current injection into the
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #RP2040's protection diodes to safe levels (~120µA), it creates a voltage divider against the C64's
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #internal pull-ups.
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #• Result: If the C64 has a strong pull-up (e.g., 1kΩ), your 10k series resistor means you
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #can never pull the line truly Low (Logic Low will be ~0.45V at the pin, but higher at the C64
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #side).
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #• Recommendation: Use N-channel MOSFETs (2N7000) or a transistor array (ULN2803) for the
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #Open Drain outputs to safely switch 5V.
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #2. Shift Register Speed vs. 10k Protection
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #• The Setup: 74HC165 powered at 5V, reading into RP2040 via 10k resistors.
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #• The Issue: 10kΩ series resistance combined with pin/trace capacitance creates a Low-Pass
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #Filter.
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #• Impact: To beat the bus, you need to clock the shift registers fast (likely >20MHz PIO
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #clock to fit 8 shifts + latch overhead into the valid data window). The RC time constant of the 10k
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #resistors might round off your square waves, causing bit errors at high speeds.
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #• Better Fix: Power the 74HC165s at 3.3V.
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #    *   74HC inputs at 3.3V VCC trigger High at ~2.3V. C64 TTL Highs are >2.4V. This is compatible.
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Output will be 3.3V (safe for RP2040).
109fc1be [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Eliminates the 10k resistors on the data lines, allowing maximum PIO speed.
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #3. Pinout & Netlist Observations
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #• GP29 (DOT Clock): You listed `GP29` for the DOT clock.
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #       Note:* If you are using a Raspberry Pi Pico board, GP29 is used internally
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #for VSYS monitoring and is not exposed as a standard GPIO pad. If you are using a raw RP2040 chip
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #or a different breakout board, this is fine.
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #• GP27 Conflict: The list shows `GP27, /DMA out`, but the summary mentions `GP26: ADC0`.
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #Just ensure you aren't expecting to use ADC functionality on the digital logic pins.
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #• 74LVC245: Wiring looks correct. 3.3V VCC on LVC is the correct way to interface 3.3V
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #logic to a 5V bus (inputs are 5V tolerant, 3.3V output drives TTL inputs fine).
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #4. Optimized PIO Strategy
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #With the 4x parallel data lines (GP17-20), your PIO program can read the entire bus in 8 cycles.
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #• Mapping: Map `IN` pins to start at GP17 (count 4).
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #• Side-set: Map `SIDESET` to GP15 (CLK).
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #• Set: Map `SET` to GP16 (SH/LD).
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #If you need the PIO assembly code for this parallel capture, let me know.
109fc1bf [gemini-3-pro] #
