109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Toast looks like a viable architecture for sniffing and injecting data onto the C64 bus,
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #particularly by leveraging the RP2040's PIO for the parallel shift register readout.
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #Here are a few technical observations regarding the netlist and electrical safety:
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #• 1. RP2040 5V Tolerance (Critical)*
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #The RP2040 GPIOs are not 5V tolerant.
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #• Open Drain Outputs (GP10–14, GP22, GP27): When driving lines like `/IRQ` or `/EXROM`,
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #setting the GPIO to High-Z allows the C64 pull-ups to pull the line to 5V. This exceeds the
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #RP2040's V_MAX. While the 10kΩ series resistors mentioned in your summary will limit the current
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #flowing into the RP2040's internal clamping diodes, this relies on those diodes for voltage
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #clamping. A dedicated level shifter or discrete N-channel MOSFETs would be electrically safer.
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #• 74HC165 Inputs: Since the shift registers are powered at 3V3 but receiving 5V logic from
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #the C64, the 10kΩ series resistors are essential to protect the 74HC inputs (clamping to VCC).
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #• 2. Bus Contention*
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #• GP21 (/OE): Ensure the logic driving the 74LVC245 Output Enable is tightly synchronized
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #with the C64's `R/W` line and `PHI2` clock. Driving D0–D7 while the VIC-II or CPU is also driving
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #the bus will cause short circuits.
109fe003 [gemini-3-pro] #
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #• 3. PIO Optimization*
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #• GP17–GP20: Wiring the `Q7` outputs of the four shift registers to contiguous GPIO pins is
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #an excellent design choice. It allows a single PIO `IN` instruction to capture Address, Data, and
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #Control lines simultaneously after the registers are clocked.
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #• 4. Clock Inputs*
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #• GP26 & GP28: The voltage divider (2.2K / 3.3K) correctly steps 5V down to ~3V, which is
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #safe for the RP2040 inputs.
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #If you require a PIO snippet to handle the shift register clocking and reading, please ask.
109fe004 [gemini-3-pro] #
