10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #Using 2N7000 FETs is a highly recommended upgrade over driving the Open Drain signals
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #directly from the RP2040.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #Why the 2N7000 is better
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Voltage Safety: The RP2040 GPIOs are not 5V tolerant. The C64 control lines
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #(IRQ, NMI, etc.) are pulled up to 5V on the C64 motherboard. Connecting these directly to the
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #RP2040, even in Open Drain mode, risks damaging the Pico because the voltage exceeds the internal
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #protection diode rating. The 2N7000 isolates the 3.3V RP2040 from the 5V C64 bus completely.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Current Handling: It offloads the sinking current from the CPU to the FET.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #Implementation Notes
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #• Logic Inversion: Using an N-Channel FET in this configuration inverts your software
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #logic.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   GPIO HIGH (3.3V) → FET ON → Drain pulls C64 line LOW.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   GPIO LOW (0V) → FET OFF → Drain floats → C64 line pulled HIGH (by C64
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #internal resistors).
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pinout: Ensure the TO-92 pinout is mapped correctly: Source to GND, Gate to GPIO, Drain
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #to C64 Pin.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #Critical Observation on 74HC165 (Shift Registers)
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #You are powering the 74HC165s at 3.3V (`VCC, 3V3` in netlist), but feeding them 5V
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #signals from the C64.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #• The Risk: The 74HC series input diodes will clamp the 5V signals down to ~3.9V, dumping
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #current into your 3.3V rail.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #• The Fix: The "10kΩ series resistors" mentioned in your summary are mandatory here
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #to limit that current.
10a01879 [gemini-3-pro] #• Timing Warning: 10kΩ is a high value for a data bus. Combined with input capacitance,
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #this creates a low-pass filter that might "smear" the edges of the 1MHz signals, potentially
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #causing data sampling errors.
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #       Recommendation:* If you miss data, try lowering those series resistors to
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #1kΩ or 2.2kΩ. This is still enough to protect the diodes but improves signal
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #rise/fall times.
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #Updated Netlist wiring for 2N7000
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #Here is how the netlist looks with the FETs added to the Open Drain lines.
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] ### 8x 2N7000 FETs (Open Drain Drivers)
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] ## Logic: GPIO HIGH = Signal LOW (Active)
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #6.1,  /IRQ,   Gate: GP10, Source: GND, Drain: C64_IRQ
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #6.2,  /NMI,   Gate: GP11, Source: GND, Drain: C64_NMI
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #6.3,  /ROML,  Gate: GP12, Source: GND, Drain: C64_ROML
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #6.4,  /ROMH,  Gate: GP13, Source: GND, Drain: C64_ROMH
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #6.5,  /EXROM, Gate: GP14, Source: GND, Drain: C64_EXROM
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #6.6,  /GAME,  Gate: GP22, Source: GND, Drain: C64_GAME
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #6.7,  /DMA,   Gate: GP27, Source: GND, Drain: C64_DMA
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #6.8,  Spare,  Reserved
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0187a [gemini-3-pro] #
