10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #Yes, the Commodore 1540 was the disk drive released for the VIC-20. It is physically almost
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #identical to the 1541, but the ROM code runs the serial bus slightly faster. The C64's VIC-II video
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #chip steals cycles from the CPU, making the C64 too slow to keep up with a 1540 (unless the screen
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #is blanked), which led to the slowed-down 1541.
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #Regarding the RP2040 PIO: It runs at system clock speed (default 125MHz). It can sample or
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #toggle pins every cycle (8ns). It is vastly faster than the IEC bus (which operates in the kHz
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #range).
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #Dropping the shift register is the right choice here. The IEC bus only has 3 main signal lines
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #(plus Reset and SRQ), so you have plenty of GPIOs on the Pico to connect them directly.
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the updated project structure for a direct-connect IEC emulator.
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Fifteen
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b963 [gemini-3-pro] #An RP2040 emulator for the Commodore Serial Bus (IEC), acting as a device (like a 1541) or
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #controller.
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #[IEC Bus 5V] ↔ [Voltage Dividers / FETs] ↔ [RP2040]
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #Architecture Change
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• Removed: 74HC165 Shift Register (Not needed, IEC is slow enough for direct GPIO, and pin
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #count is low).
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• Added: Voltage Dividers for Input (Reading 5V IEC lines safely).
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• Kept: 2N7000 FETs for Output (Driving Open Collector IEC lines).
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #BOM
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• 5x 2N7000 N-Channel FET (Output drivers for ATN, CLK, DATA, SRQ, RESET)
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• 5x 2.2kΩ Resistors (Input Divider Series)
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• 5x 3.3kΩ Resistors (Input Divider to GND)
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• 2x DIN 45322 6-pin connectors (IEC ports)
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• 1x RP2040 (Pico)
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #• 2x 20-pin female header
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #GPIO Interface Logic
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #The IEC bus is Open Collector with pull-ups on the host/drive side.
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Reading (Input):
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   IEC Line (5V) → 2.2kΩ → GPIO Input → 3.3kΩ → GND.
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Logic High at IEC (5V) ≈ 3.0V at GPIO (Safe logic 1).
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Writing (Output):
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   GPIO Output → Gate of 2N7000.
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Source → GND.
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Drain → IEC Line.
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Logic: High on GPIO pulls IEC Line LOW.
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #Netlist Draft
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #IEC Connector Pinout (Looking at C64 port)
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  SRQ (Fast Serial / Service Request)
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  GND
10a0b964 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  ATN (Attention)
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #4.  CLK (Clock)
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #5.  DATA
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #6.  RESET
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #GPIO Allocation
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #╭────────────────┬─────────────┬───────────┬────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  Signal        │  Direction  │  Logic    │  GPIO  │  Description                                            │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #├────────────────┼─────────────┼───────────┼────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  :---          │  :---       │  :---     │  :---  │  :---                                                   │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_ATN**   │  IN         │  Divider  │  GP2   │  Host requesting attention                              │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_ATN**   │  OUT        │  FET      │  GP3   │  Device acknowledging (rare, usually host drives this)  │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_CLK**   │  IN         │  Divider  │  GP4   │  Clock line state                                       │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_CLK**   │  OUT        │  FET      │  GP5   │  Drive pulling clock low                                │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_DATA**  │  IN         │  Divider  │  GP6   │  Data line state                                        │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_DATA**  │  OUT        │  FET      │  GP7   │  Drive pulling data low                                 │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_SRQ**   │  IN         │  Divider  │  GP8   │  Fast Serial state                                      │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_SRQ**   │  OUT        │  FET      │  GP9   │  Fast Serial drive                                      │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_RST**   │  IN         │  Divider  │  GP10  │  System Reset state                                     │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #│  **IEC_RST**   │  OUT        │  FET      │  GP11  │  Drive resetting bus                                    │
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #╰────────────────┴─────────────┴───────────┴────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
10a0b965 [gemini-3-pro] #
