10a0cffc [nitro@ryzen5] add ATN so 4 fet?
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #Yes, the Commodore 1540 was the disk drive produced for the VIC-20. It uses a slightly
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #faster serial timing than the 1541. The C64 actually has to slow down its bus timing to talk to a
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #1541; the 1540 is generally incompatible with a stock C64 because the C64 CPU halts during video
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #line blanking, missing bits at 1540 speeds.
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #• PIO Speed:*
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #The RP2040 PIO runs at system clock (default 125MHz). It can shift data in/out at tens of megabytes
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #per second. The Commodore IEC bus runs at roughly 1.2kHz to 2.4kHz (Standard) or ~10-20kHz (Fast
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #Serial). The PIO is orders of magnitude faster than necessary; it can bit-bang IEC while sleeping.
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #• Signals to Drive:*
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #The IEC bus is Open Collector (Open Drain).
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #1.  DATA: Drive Low (Acknowledge/Data).
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #2.  CLK: Drive Low (Handshake/Clock).
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #3.  ATN: Drive Low (Only if acting as Master/Host). A Drive usually only reads ATN.
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #4.  SRQ: Drive Low (Fast Serial / Burst Mode). Used by 1571/1581/C128.
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #• 4 FETs?*
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #Yes. To be fully compliant (Fast Serial capable + Host capable), you need 4.
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #If simulating a standard 1541 only: 2 FETs (Data, Clk).
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #If simulating a 1581 or Host: 4 FETs (Data, Clk, Atn, Srq).
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the updated project spec dropping the shift registers for direct GPIO.
10a0d2ed [gemini-3-pro] #
