10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #Yes, the Commodore 1540 was the disk drive designed for the VIC-20. It is electrically compatible
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #with the C64 but runs slightly faster than the 1541.
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #Regarding your technical questions:
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #1.  PIO Speed: The RP2040 PIO can run at the system clock speed (125MHz+). It is
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #significantly faster than the IEC bus (Standard ~2.4kB/s, Fast ~10kB/s) and can easily handle
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #bit-banging or serialization without shift registers.
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #2.  UART Pins: Yes, on the RP2040 (Pico), GP0 is UART0 TX and GP1 is UART0
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #RX. To keep these available for USB/Serial debugging, I have mapped the IEC bus starting at GP2
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #below.
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the updated project definition.
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42c [gemini-3-pro] #Project FifteenA
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #A RP2040 hookup for Commodore Serial Bus (IEC) emulation using direct GPIO manipulation
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #(Bit-banging/PIO).
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #[USB] ─ RP2040 ─ [Level Shifting] ─ DIN-6 Socket ─ [C64]
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #BOM
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #4x 2N7000 N-Channel FET ($0.40) - Open Drain Drivers for ATN, DATA, CLK, SRQ
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #2x DIN 45322 6-pin female connectors ($3.50) - IEC Bus
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #5x 2.2kΩ Resistors (Input Divider Series)
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #5x 3.3kΩ Resistors (Input Divider to GND)
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #1x 20-pin female header, Pico socket
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #5x 100nF ceramic cap (decoupling)
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #GPIO Logic
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #• Inputs (Reading 5V Bus):
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Voltage Divider: IEC_PIN (5V) → 2.2kΩ → GPIO → 3.3kΩ → GND.
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Logic: Bus High (~5V) = GPIO High (~3.0V).
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #• Outputs (Driving Bus Low):
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #    *   2N7000 FET: Gate to GPIO, Source to GND, Drain to IEC_PIN.
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Logic: GPIO HIGH = FET ON = IEC LOW (Active).
10a0f42d [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Logic: GPIO LOW = FET OFF = IEC FLOAT (Passive High via C64 pullups).
