10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #These are solid designs. A few observations:
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #• node.md* - For the user port edge connector, the EDAC 395-024-520-202 is correct. Note
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #it's 0.156" (3.96mm) pitch. You'll want to confirm the PCB edge thickness spec (typically 1.6mm
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #works).
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #• toast.md* - The 74LVC245 running at 3V3 driving into 5V C64 data bus might need
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #consideration. The C64 expects VOH around 2.4V minimum which 3V3 logic meets, but you're reading
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #back via the 165s - watch for bus contention if the C64 is also driving the data lines. The /OE
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #gating on GP21 handles this if timed to PHI2 correctly.
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #• fifteen.md* - Clean IEC design. Missing /RESET output driver? You have input on GP6 but
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #no FET to assert it. Might want a 5th 2N7000 if you need to reset peripherals.
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #• luma2.md* - The 220K bias resistors from GPIO to trimpot wipers - is that for calibration
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #via software? Clever if so. The LM319 is fast enough for the ~8MHz dot clock bandwidth you'd need
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #for 320px capture.
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #Any specific area you want to dig into?
10a164ba [claude-opus-4-5] #
