10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #Yes, same approach works. For CIA2 Port B (PB0-PB7):
10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #• Reading from C64:* 10K series resistors to GPIO (static signals, not clock speed)
10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #• Writing to C64:* 74LVC245 with /OE gating, or 8x 2N7000 open drain if you only need to
10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #pull low
10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #The user port is bidirectional per-pin via CIA2 DDRB register, so you need to handle both
10a16cb3 [claude-opus-4-5] #directions. Simplest is:
