10a1a4b6 [nitro@ryzen5] what is SP2?
10a1a538 [claude-opus-4-5] #SP2 is CIA2's second serial port data line.
10a1a538 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a1a538 [claude-opus-4-5] #CIA2 has two independent serial shift registers:
10a1a538 [claude-opus-4-5] #- SP1/CNT1 - Serial Port 1 data/clock
10a1a539 [claude-opus-4-5] #- SP2/CNT2 - Serial Port 2 data/clock
10a1a539 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a1a539 [claude-opus-4-5] #Each can shift 8 bits in or out, clocked by its CNT line. Used for fast serial protocols - much
10a1a539 [claude-opus-4-5] #quicker than the software-bitbanged IEC bus.
10a1a539 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a1a539 [claude-opus-4-5] #Common uses:
10a1a539 [claude-opus-4-5] #- Fast disk loaders (e.g. SpeedDOS, JiffyDOS parallel cable)
