10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #• FLAG2* - CIA2 input only. External device pulls low to signal "data ready". Directly
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #triggers CIA interrupt. C64 cannot drive it.
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #• PC2* - CIA2 output only. Directly controlled by C64 to signal "byte taken". Directly
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #triggers CIA interrupt. C64 pulses it automatically on Port B read/write.
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #So:
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #- FLAG2 - input to C64, output from Pico → needs 2N7000
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #- PC2 - output from C64, input to Pico → shift register only
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a223a9 [claude-opus-4-5] #GP19,FLAG2 out,Output,2N7000,B
