10a2762b [nitro@ryzen5] will the luma2 comparators run that fast?
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #LM319 is only guaranteed to 80 ns (≈ 12 MHz) propagation delay typical, 150 ns max over
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #temperature.
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #At 14 MHz PAL sub-carrier one cycle is 71 ns, so the 319 barely keeps up and the phase error gives
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #you ±15° hue noise. That is still enough to separate VIC-II colours because they’re spaced 45°
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #apart, but you have to:
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #- Run the 319 from 5 V (gives you the fastest output edges)
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #- Keep the input overdrive > 100 mV (use a 1 kΩ pull-up on the open-collector output so it swings
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #0–5 V)
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #- Sample on the next PIO edge so you always see the same 80 ns pipeline delay
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #If you want a safety margin, swap one 319 for an LMV7219 (8 ns) or just use the zero-cross counter
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #trick—then the 319 only toggles at colour-burst frequency and the timing is trivial.
10a27715 [kimi-k2-0905] #
