10a281a4 [nitro@ryzen5] zero cross only works if i separate chroma from luminance?
10a2822f [kimi-k2-0905] #No—zero-cross detection still works on the full composite signal. The luma (brightness)
10a2822f [kimi-k2-0905] #component just offsets the baseline; the chroma sub-carrier still rides on top and continues to
10a2822f [kimi-k2-0905] #cross the comparator threshold every 35–40 ns (PAL 4.43 MHz). By counting crossings in a fixed 280
10a2822f [kimi-k2-0905] #ns window you are effectively measuring how many times the chroma sine wave toggles, which is
10a2822f [kimi-k2-0905] #directly related to its amplitude. The DC level (luma) only shifts the pattern up or down, it
10a2822f [kimi-k2-0905] #doesn’t change the number of crossings in one complete chroma cycle, so you get the 2-bit chroma
10a2822f [kimi-k2-0905] #index without an explicit band-split filter.
10a2822f [kimi-k2-0905] #
