10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #Set the comparator threshold to black level (≈ 0.3 V, or 7.5 IRE) and keep it there—do
10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #not chase the instantaneous luma.
10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #Because the chroma sine wave is AC-coupled (±0.15 V typical), every time it swings above 0.3 V and
10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #then back below 0.3 V you get one logic transition on the comparator output.
10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #Those edges are exactly the zero-crossings of the chroma sub-carrier.
10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #Counting them in hardware (RP2040 PIO):
10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10a28b46 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. Route the comparator digital output to a PIO input pin.
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. In one PIO state-machine:
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #   set x, 13          ; 13 edges = 1 PAL chroma cycle (280 ns)
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #wait_edge:
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #   wait 1 pin         ; wait for high
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #   wait 0 pin         ; wait for low
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #   jmp x-- wait_edge  ; decrement and loop
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #   in isr, 1          ; push final count
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. The count left in the ISR is 0, 1 or 2 → map to 2-bit chroma index.
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #Luma changes only shift the whole sine vertically; as long as the amplitude is > 100 mV the
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #comparator still toggles the same number of times per chroma cycle, so you get the colour ID for
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #free without filtering.
10a28b47 [kimi-k2-0905] #
