10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #Issues Found
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #1. 74HC165 VCC voltage mismatch - U1 and U2 show `VCC, 5V` but they're feeding GP19/GP20
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #directly. The 74HC165 outputs will be 5V logic levels going into 3.3V GPIOs without protection.
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #Either:
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #   - Use 74LVC165 (3.3V tolerant) instead
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #   - Add 10K series resistors on Q7 outputs
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #   - Run 74HC165 from 3V3 (may affect input thresholds from 5V C64 signals)
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a4119e [claude-opus-4-5] #2. Shift register clock/load pins - GP17 is CLK, GP18 is SH/LD in the GPIO table, but the
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #74HC165 pinouts show the same assignment. That's consistent, good.
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #3. CNT1/CNT2 dual routing - These signals appear in both:
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #   - Shift register U2 (P4, P5) for static reads
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #   - Voltage dividers to GP26/GP27 for fast clock capture
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #   This is fine if intentional (PIO on GP26/27 for timing, shift reg for state polling).
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #4. Missing series protection - The shift register parallel inputs (PB0-7, SP1, SP2, PA2,
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #FLAG2, CNT1, CNT2, PC2) connect directly to 5V C64 signals. The 74HC165 is 5V tolerant on inputs
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #when powered at 5V, so this is OK.
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a4119f [claude-opus-4-5] #5. PC2 direction - Listed as input to shift register, but PC2 is a CIA output
