10a44c0a [claude-opus-4-5] #• Fifteen* - Solid. Simple and proven approach. No issues.
10a44c0a [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a44c0a [claude-opus-4-5] #• LUMA2* - Timing is tight. 280ns chroma window at 125MHz gives ~35 cycles. PIO edge
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #counting feasible but needs careful tuning. Bias resistor through GPIO (220K) is unconventional -
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #works but adds coupling between threshold adjustment and Pico state.
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #• Toast* - PHI2 at ~1MHz through voltage divider is marginal. 3.3K to ground with cable
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #capacitance may round edges. Consider lower divider impedance (1K/1.5K). Also reading control
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #signals through shift register adds 8+ clock latencies - fine for slow signals, problematic if
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #timing ROM responses to PHI2.
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #• Node* - 74HC165 running at 5V with Q7 through 10K to 3.3V GPIO is borderline. HC outputs
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #swing to VCC, so you're relying on the 10K plus GPIO clamp diodes. Works but not ideal. Consider
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #74LVC165 at 3.3V or proper level shifter. CNT1/CNT2 dividers are correct for clock inputs.
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #• Common issue*: No protection on 2N7000 gates if 5V backfeeds during power sequencing. 10K
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #gate resistors would add safety margin.
10a44c0b [claude-opus-4-5] #
