10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #This is a comprehensive suite of retro-computing interfaces for the RP2040.
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #• Project Crumpet (Sega Megadrive) and cbm node* (C64 User Port) appear to be the
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #newest additions compared to previous iterations of this list.
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #Here are a few technical observations regarding the new and updated designs:
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Crumpet (Megadrive)
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #• Timing Constraints: The Megadrive 68k bus runs at ~7.67 MHz. Using shift registers
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #(74HC165/595) to read the Address Bus and write the Data Bus introduces significant serialization
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #latency.
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   This design is excellent for a Cartridge Dumper or Bus Logic Analyzer.
10a8b660 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   It is likely too slow for Real-time ROM Emulation. The time required to shift in 24
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #address bits + control lines, process, and shift out 16 data bits will exceed the bus read cycle
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #window.
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #• GPIO Allocation: `GP12` is listed as `shift out, QH D0-d7`. Assuming this drives the
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #`SER` (Serial Data Input) of the 74HC595 chain, the netlist looks consistent for a serial setup.
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Toast (C64 Cartridge)
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #• Latency: Similar to Crumpet, while the C64 bus is slower (1 MHz), the valid data window
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #during PHI2 high is roughly 450-500ns. Serializing address reads via shift registers consumes a
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #large portion of this budget, leaving very little time for the RP2040 to fetch data and stabilize
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #the transceivers.
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #Project cbm node (User Port)
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #• Viability: This is a very robust design. The User Port (CIA2) generally handles
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #handshake-driven or slower asynchronous communications, making the shift-register approach
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #perfectly viable here compared to the system bus projects.
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #• BOM/Netlist: The mixture of 165s for inputs and 245s for parallel output (PB0-PB7) is
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #well-optimized for the bidirectional nature of the User Port.
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #Project LUMA2 (Chroma Mod)
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #• Zero-Cross: Adding the AC coupling and comparator for zero-crossing detection (`GP6`) to
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #capture Chroma phase information is a significant functional upgrade over the pure Luma capture.
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Fifteen (IEC)
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #• Logic: The open-drain FET logic combined with voltage dividers for inputs is the
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #standard, reliable method for 3.3V logic interfacing with the 5V IEC bus.
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #The netlists are well-structured for PCB generation. If the intent for Toast and
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #Crumpet is real-time emulation, you may need to switch from shift registers to direct GPIO
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #parallel access (requiring pin multiplexing or larger MCUs) to meet bus timing.
10a8b661 [gemini-3-pro] #
