10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #Thank you for sharing the specifications for Project Crumpet. I have added the Sega
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #Megadrive interface to the context alongside Project Fifteen, LUMA2, Toast, and the CBM node.
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #Here are a few observations regarding the new content, specifically concerning the "8 shifts"
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #constraint and the BOM:
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #1. Parallel Output Logic (D0–D15)
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #To achieve the 16-bit write (D0–D15) in only 8 clock cycles, the two 74HC595 shift
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #registers must be fed in parallel, not daisy-chained.
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Current GPIO: `GP12` is assigned to `shift out, QH D0-d7`.
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Missing GPIO: You will likely need a specific GPIO assigned to the second 74HC595
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #(D8–D15) serial input (DS pin).
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Logic: The PIO would output 2 bits per clock (one to GP12, one to the new pin) to fill
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #both registers simultaneously in 8 cycles.
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #2. Bus Contention & Output Enable
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #Unlike Project Toast (which uses 74LVC245 transceivers), Project Crumpet uses
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #74HC595s for output.
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Risk: 74HC595 outputs are always active unless the `/OE` (Output Enable) pin is high. If
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #the Megadrive CPU and the '595s drive the data bus simultaneously, it causes a short.
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Recommendation: Ensure the `/OE` pins of the 74HC595s are controlled by the RP2040 (or
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #logic tied to the Megadrive's `R/W` line) so the shift registers are High-Z when the RP2040 is
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #reading via the 74HC165s.
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #3. Input Capacity Check
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #You have 6× 74HC165 registers (48 bits total capacity).
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Address: 23 bits (A1–A23).
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Data: 16 bits (D0–D15).
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Control: ~9 bits available.
10a8bb00 [gemini-3-pro] #• Total: 48 bits.
10a8bb01 [gemini-3-pro] #This fits perfectly into the 6 parallel input streams (GP4–GP9) over 8 clocks.
10a8bb01 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8bb01 [gemini-3-pro] #The project definitions are stored. I am ready for code requests or further refinements.
10a8bb01 [gemini-3-pro] #
