10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Crumpet looks like a robust solution for the high pin count of the 16-bit era. The update
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #to the GPIO allocation for parallel shifting is a significant optimization; reducing the read
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #operation to 8 clock cycles (reading 6 bits wide) and the write operation to 8 clock cycles
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #(writing 2 bits wide) will drastically improve timing margins against the ~7.6MHz bus.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #Here are a few observations on the updated Netlist and BOM:
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• BOM vs. Summary Discrepancy*
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• Summary: Mentions `2x74LVC245` transceivers.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• BOM/Netlist: Lists `2x 74HC595` shift registers for the output stage.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• Note: If the plan is to drive the 5V data bus via shift registers, ensure you use
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #74HCT595 (TTL inputs) if powering them at 5V. Standard HC chips at 5V may not reliably
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #detect the RP2040's 3.3V logic high. Alternatively, the LVC245s mentioned in the summary would
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #handle level translation perfectly if placed between the 3.3V logic and the bus.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• Logic Logic*
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• Input Coverage: 6 × 74HC165 provides 48 bits of input.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Address (23) + Data (16) = 39 bits.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   This leaves 9 bits for control signals (/AS, /DTACK, etc.), which fits perfectly.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• Output Coverage: 2 × 74HC595 provides 16 bits of output.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   This covers D0–D15 exactly.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• Updated GPIO Allocation*
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #The updated pinout for the output stage looks correct for the parallel write strategy:
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• GP10 (CLK) / GP11 (SH/LD) / GP12 (OE): Shared control lines.
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• GP13 / GP14: Data lines feeding two shift registers simultaneously (High Byte / Low
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #Byte).
10a8cfa1 [gemini-3-pro] #• GP15: Reserved for the incoming system clock.
10a8cfa2 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8cfa2 [gemini-3-pro] #The documentation has been updated.
10a8cfa2 [gemini-3-pro] #
