10a8dfd6 [gemini-3-pro] #FET Control Logic
10a8dfd6 [gemini-3-pro] #The two signals that require Open Drain driving (Active Low) on a Megadrive cartridge are:
10a8dfd6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8dfd6 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  /DTACK (Pin B31): Data Acknowledge. The console waits for this to go LOW before
10a8dfd6 [gemini-3-pro] #finishing a bus cycle. Driving this allows the RP2040 to pause the 68k if it needs more time to
10a8dfd6 [gemini-3-pro] #fetch data.
10a8dfd6 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  /CART (Pin B32): Cartridge Detect. Usually tied to GND. Driving this allows the RP2040
10a8dfd7 [gemini-3-pro] #to simulate cartridge insertion/removal electronically.
