10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #Emulation Cycle Steps (CSV)
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the logical flow for a Read Cycle using shift registers, relying on /DTACK to pause the
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #CPU.
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #Step,Action,Signals,Description
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #1,Idle,GP16=LOW(Float); GP12=HIGH,Wait for start of cycle (monitor CLK/CS)
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #2,Capture,GP3=LOW; GP3=HIGH,Pulse SH/LD to parallel load 74HC165 inputs
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #3,Shift In,GP2 cycles 8 times,Read 6 bits simultaneously (Addresses + Control)
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #4,Decode,Internal Logic,Reconstruct 24-bit Address and check Control bits (/CE /AS)
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #5,Lookup,Internal Logic,Fetch 16-bit word from ROM array based on Address
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #6,Shift Out,GP10 cycles 8 times,Push 16-bit Data to 74HC595 (GP13/GP14)
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #7,Latch Out,GP11=HIGH; GP11=LOW,Move shifted data to storage register
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #8,Bus Drive,GP12=LOW,Enable 74HC595 Output (Put Data on Bus)
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #9,Ack,GP16=HIGH(Active Low),Turn on FET to pull /DTACK Low (CPU resumes)
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #10,Hold,Wait for Control High,Wait for /AS or /CE to go High (Cycle End)
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #11,Release,GP12=HIGH; GP16=LOW(Float),Disable 74HC595 Output; Release /DTACK
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #Timing Feasibility Analysis
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #• Is Crumpet timing ok?*
10a8fa8b [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #• Yes, but only because of /DTACK.*
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #1.  The Challenge: The 68000 bus cycle is roughly 500ns-600ns. Using shift registers
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #creates significant latency.
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Shift In (8 clocks) + Processing + Shift Out (8 clocks) will likely exceed the standard ROM
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #access window of a real cartridge (~200ns).
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #2.  The Solution: The Sega Genesis/Megadrive respects the /DTACK line.
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The CPU will enter "Wait States" automatically if /DTACK is not asserted immediately.
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #    *   By leaving /DTACK floating (High) until the RP2040 has finished shifting bits in and out,
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #you effectively pause the console.
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Constraint: You must ensure the RP2040 PIO is clocked high enough (e.g., >125MHz) to
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #minimize the wait states, otherwise audio glitching (which relies on CPU timing) or raster effects
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #might desync.
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Signal Integrity: Ensure the 74HC595 Output Enable (GP12) is strictly managed. You must
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #not drive the data bus until you are sure it is a Read cycle, otherwise, you risk bus contention
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #(short circuit) if the CPU tries to write at the same time.
10a8fa8c [gemini-3-pro] #
