10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the breakdown for the FET drivers, the emulation sequence, and the timing analysis for
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #Project Crumpet.
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #FET Drivers
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #The Megadrive bus relies on Open Drain signals for handshaking and presence detection.
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #1.  /DTACK (Data Acknowledge): Essential. The cartridge must pull this low to tell
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #the 68000 that data is valid on the bus. If this is not driven low, the console will hang (wait
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #state).
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #2.  /CART (Cartridge Detect): Required. This must be pulled low for the I/O
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #controller to enable the cartridge slot power/logic.
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #• Netlist update for FETs:*
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #• Q1 (/DTACK): Gate: GP16, Source: GND, Drain: B32 (/DTACK)
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #• Q2 (/CART): Gate: GP17, Source: GND, Drain: B32 (/CART) - Note: often pin B32, verify
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #specific edge connector pinout.
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #Emulation Sequence (Read Cycle)
10a900cd [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #The following CSV details the steps the RP2040 must perform to emulate a ROM read cycle.
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #Step,Action,Direction,Signal,Description
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #1,Wait,Input,/AS,Wait for 68k to pull Address Strobe LOW
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #2,Latch,Output,SH/LD,Pulse 74HC165 SH/LD to capture bus state
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #3,Shift In,Input,Q7 Lanes,PIO clocks 8 times to read Address (A1-A23) and Control
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #4,Process,Internal,RP2040,Decode Address and fetch 16-bit Data word
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #5,Shift Out,Output,SER/CLK,PIO shifts 16-bit Data into 74HC595s
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #6,Output Enable,Output,/OE,Enable 74HC595 outputs to drive D0-D15
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #7,Handshake,Output,/DTACK,Drive GP16 HIGH (FET pulls /DTACK LOW)
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #8,Hold,Input,/AS,Wait for 68k to release Address Strobe HIGH
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #9,Release,Output,/DTACK,Drive GP16 LOW (FET releases /DTACK to High-Z)
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #10,Disable,Output,/OE,Disable 74HC595 outputs (High-Z)
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #Timing Analysis
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #• Is Crumpet timing ok?*
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #• Yes, but it is tight.*
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #• Bus Speed: The 68000 runs at ~7.67 MHz. One clock cycle is ~130ns.
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #• Access Window: A standard bus cycle is 4 clocks (~520ns). The time from `/AS` going low
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #to data setup required is roughly 250ns.
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #• Propagation Delay:
10a900ce [gemini-3-pro] #    *   74HC165 Latch/Shift: ~25ns
