10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #To facilitate writing from the RP2040 to the 68K data bus (D0-D15) using two 74LVC245 transceivers,
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #please consider the following hardware and logic configuration:
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #• Power Supply: Power the 74LVC245 transceivers at 3.3V. The LVC family is 5V
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #tolerant on inputs, and the 3.3V output high level is sufficient to trigger standard 68000 TTL
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #inputs (V_IH \ge 2.0V).
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #• Port Mapping: Connect the RP2040 GPIOs to the A ports and the 68K data lines to
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #the B ports.
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #• Direction Control (DIR): Drive the DIR pin High to route data from A (RP2040) to
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #B (68K).
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #• Output Enable (\overlineOE): Drive the \overlineOE pin Low to enable the outputs.
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #Ensure this pin is pulled High (Hi-Z state) whenever the RP2040 is not actively performing a write
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #cycle to prevent bus contention.
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #• Control Signals: You must synchronize the transceiver activation with the 68K bus control
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #signals, specifically asserting R/\overlineW low (Write) and managing address strobes (\overlineAS,
10a99d0a [gemini-3-pro] #\overlineUDS, \overlineLDS).
