10a9a9e1 [nitro@ryzen5] # descriptionGangs of shift registers transport data between millenium.The RP2040 PIO empties shift registers in parallel so only 8 cycles required.Once address decoded and confirmation write cycle is required data is place on megadrive bus with some buffers?
10a9aaf1 [gemini-3-pro] #Based on your specifications, here is a description of the hardware interface and data flow:
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #• System Architecture*
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #The design interfaces an RP2040 microcontroller with a Motorola 68000-based system (Mega Drive)
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #using shift registers for data transport and transceivers for bus isolation.
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #• Operational Flow*
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Data Ingestion: The RP2040 PIO state machines read the "gangs" of shift registers in
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #parallel. This parallelization allows the microcontroller to empty the registers and reconstruct
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #the data word in just 8 clock cycles.
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Bus Interface: Two 74LVC245 transceivers manage the 16-bit data bus (D0-D15). These
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #devices serve as bidirectional buffers and voltage level translators between the RP2040 and the 5V
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #system.
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Bus Access:
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   External logic or the RP2040 performs address decoding to detect a valid bus cycle.
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Once a write cycle is confirmed, the RP2040 asserts the Output Enable (OE) and Direction
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #(DIR) pins on the 74LVC245s.
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The buffered data is then actively driven onto the Mega Drive bus for the 68000 to access.
10a9aaf2 [gemini-3-pro] #
