10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #You need 8 pins for data, plus 3 control pins (Clock Low, Clock High, Output Enable).
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #╭────────────┬────────────────────┬─────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────╮
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  GPIO      │  Function          │  Direction  │  Note                               │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #├────────────┼────────────────────┼─────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────┤
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  :---      │  :---              │  :---       │  :---                               │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP10**  │  **MD_D0**         │  Output     │  Connect to D0 on **both** U7 & U8  │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP11**  │  **MD_D1**         │  Output     │  Connect to D1 on **both** U7 & U8  │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP12**  │  **MD_D2**         │  Output     │  Connect to D2 on **both** U7 & U8  │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP13**  │  **MD_D3**         │  Output     │  Connect to D3 on **both** U7 & U8  │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP14**  │  **MD_D4**         │  Output     │  Connect to D4 on **both** U7 & U8  │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP15**  │  **MD_D5**         │  Output     │  Connect to D5 on **both** U7 & U8  │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP16**  │  **MD_D6**         │  Output     │  Connect to D6 on **both** U7 & U8  │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP17**  │  **MD_D7**         │  Output     │  Connect to D7 on **both** U7 & U8  │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP21**  │  **LATCH_CLK_LO**  │  Output     │  Clocks data into Low Byte 374      │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP22**  │  **LATCH_CLK_HI**  │  Output     │  Clocks data into High Byte 374     │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GP26**  │  **LATCH_OE**      │  Output     │  Enables 374 outputs onto MD Bus    │
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #╰────────────┴────────────────────┴─────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────╯
10a9c52f [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• (GP18-GP20 remain as CLK_IN, /DTACK, /CART per your previous list).*
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #Netlist: 74LS374 Connections
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• U7: Low Byte Latch (D0-D7)*
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 1 (/OE): Connect to GP26 (Common OE)
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 11 (CLK): Connect to GP21 (Latch Low)
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pins 3,4,7,8,13,14,17,18 (D0-D7 Inputs): Connect to GP10-GP17
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pins 2,5,6,9,12,15,16,19 (Q0-Q7 Outputs): Connect to Megadrive D0-D7
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• U8: High Byte Latch (D8-D15)*
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 1 (/OE): Connect to GP26 (Common OE)
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 11 (CLK): Connect to GP22 (Latch High)
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pins 3,4,7,8,13,14,17,18 (D0-D7 Inputs): Connect to GP10-GP17
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pins 2,5,6,9,12,15,16,19 (Q0-Q7 Outputs): Connect to Megadrive D8-D15
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #Write Logic Sequence
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #To present 16-bit data (e.g., `0xABCD`) to the Megadrive:
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Idle: GP26 (/OE) is HIGH (High-Z state, not interfering with bus).
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Setup Low: Put `0xCD` (Low Byte) on GP10-GP17.
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Latch Low: Pulse GP21 (CLK_LO) High then Low. (U7 now holds `0xCD`).
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Setup High: Put `0xAB` (High Byte) on GP10-GP17.
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #5.  Latch High: Pulse GP22 (CLK_HI) High then Low. (U8 now holds `0xAB`).
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #6.  Drive Bus: Set GP26 (/OE) LOW. (Megadrive now sees `0xABCD`).
10a9c530 [gemini-3-pro] #7.  Handshake: Assert /DTACK (GP19 High -> FET Pulls Low).
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #8.  Finish: When Read Cycle ends, release /DTACK and set GP26 (/OE) HIGH.
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #Important Notes
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #• Bus Contention: Ensure your code logic never pulls GP26 (/OE) LOW unless you are
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #100% sure the Megadrive is performing a Read cycle. If the Megadrive tries to write while the 374s
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #are active, you will have a short circuit.
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #• Speed: This parallel method is significantly faster than the 74HC595 serial method (2 bus
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #writes vs 16 serial shifts), leaving more PIO cycles for address decoding.
10a9c531 [gemini-3-pro] #
