10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #Yes, using 74LS374 Octal D-Type Flip-Flops is the correct approach to drive a 16-bit bus
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #using only 8 data GPIOs. Unlike the '245 transceiver, the '374 has memory (latches), allowing you
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #to write the low byte, store it, write the high byte, store it, and then enable both onto the bus
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #simultaneously.
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #Since 74LS inputs are TTL compatible, the 3.3V logic high from the RP2040 is sufficient to drive
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #them while they are powered at 5V.
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the revised documentation for Project Crumpet.
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Crumpet (Revised)
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #A 16bit Sega Megadrive RP2040 hookup on plated 64 finger edge connector.
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #[USB] ─ RP2040 ─ [Shift In / Latch Out] ─ Cartridge Port ─ [Megadrive]
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #BOM Updates
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #• Remove: 2× 74LVC245 Transceivers
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #• Add: 2× 74LS374 Octal D-Type Flip-Flops (Jaycar NZ$3.00)
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #       Note:* Powered at 5V. RP2040 3.3V outputs directly drive LS TTL inputs (VIH min
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #2.0V).
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GPIO Allocation
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #• Shift Inputs (Reading)*
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP0, UART TX
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP1, UART RX
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP2, shift in CLK (Common U1-U6)
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP3, shift in SH/LD (Common U1-U6)
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP4, shift in Q7 A0-A7
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP5, shift in Q7 A8-A15
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP6, shift in Q7 A16-A23
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP7, shift in Q7 D0-D7
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP8, shift in Q7 D8-D15
10a9cc53 [gemini-3-pro] #GP9, shift in Q7 Controls
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• Multiplexed Data Output (Driving)*
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP10, Bus D0, Output (To U7/U8 Inputs)
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP11, Bus D1, Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP12, Bus D2, Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP13, Bus D3, Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP14, Bus D4, Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP15, Bus D5, Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP16, Bus D6, Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP17, Bus D7, Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• Control Signals*
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP18, CLK in, Input (2.2K/3.3K divider)
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP19, /DTACK, Output (Open Drain FET)
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP20, /CART, Output (Open Drain FET)
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP21, Latch CP Low (U7 Clock), Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP22, Latch CP High (U8 Clock), Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #GP26, /OE Output Enable (U7+U8), Output
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #Netlist Updates
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #U7 - 74LS374 (Data Low D0-D7)
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• VCC: 5V
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• GND: GND
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• D0-D7 (Inputs): Connect to RP2040 GP10-GP17
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• Q0-Q7 (Outputs): Connect to Megadrive D0-D7
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• CP (Pin 11): GP21
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #•  /OE (Pin 1): GP26
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #U8 - 74LS374 (Data High D8-D15)
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• VCC: 5V
10a9cc54 [gemini-3-pro] #• GND: GND
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #• D0-D7 (Inputs): Connect to RP2040 GP10-GP17
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #• Q0-Q7 (Outputs): Connect to Megadrive D8-D15
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #• CP (Pin 11): GP22
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #•  /OE (Pin 1): GP26
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #Emulation Logic Steps (Write Cycle)
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Idle: GP26 (/OE) is HIGH (Outputs High-Z).
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Load Low: Place lower 8 bits on GP10-GP17. Pulse GP21 (CP Low). Data is now stored in
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #U7.
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Load High: Place upper 8 bits on GP10-GP17. Pulse GP22 (CP High). Data is now stored in
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #U8.
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Drive Bus: Set GP26 (/OE) LOW. U7 and U8 drive D0-D15 onto the Megadrive bus.
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #5.  Ack: Assert /DTACK (GP19 High -> FET Low).
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #6.  Release: After bus cycle ends, set GP26 (/OE) HIGH and release /DTACK.
10a9cc55 [gemini-3-pro] #
