10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Inconsistency in Project Crumpet Output Stage:*
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  BOM & GPIO Allocation: Lists 74LS374 (Octal D-type Flip-Flops/Latches). The
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #GPIO allocation defines `GP10-GP17` as a parallel data bus ("latch d0-d7") with separate clock pins
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #(`GP18`, `GP19`) for low/high bytes. This suggests a multiplexed parallel write strategy.
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Emulation Logic Steps: Steps 5, 6, and 7 describe driving 74HC595 (Serial Shift
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #Registers). Specifically, Step 5 mentions "Clock GP10 8 times... Shift 16-bit data," and Step 7
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #explicitly names "Enable 74HC595 output drivers."
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Recommendation:*
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #• If using 74LS374 (Parallel): The Logic Steps need to be updated to reflect writing an
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #8-bit byte to `GP10-17`, pulsing `GP18` (Low Byte), writing the next byte, and pulsing `GP19` (High
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #Byte).
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #• If using 74HC595 (Serial): The BOM and GPIO allocation need to be changed to remove the
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #parallel bus pins and assign Serial Data (DS), Shift Clock (SHCP), and Store Clock (STCP) pins
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #instead.
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #The remaining projects (Fifteen, Luma2, Toast, Cbm Node) appear internally consistent regarding
10a9d5e7 [gemini-3-pro] #their BOMs and Netlists.
