10aa1c54 [gemini-3-pro] #1. GPIO / Documentation Conflict
10aa1c54 [gemini-3-pro] #There is a discrepancy regarding the Master Clock input between your Netlist and the JS
10aa1c54 [gemini-3-pro] #module:
10aa1c54 [gemini-3-pro] #• Netlist: `GP28, CLK, in, 2.2K+3.3K` (GP26/27 listed as spare).
10aa1c54 [gemini-3-pro] #• JS Module: `26: { name: "MD_CLK"... }`.
10aa1c54 [gemini-3-pro] #• Resolution: Ensure the physical PCB routing matches the code. GP26-29 are ADC pins on the
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #Pico; GP26 is valid for digital input, but GP28 is often preferred for PIO clock synchronization if
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #available.
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #2. The "U6" Control Line Shift Register
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #Your netlist defines U6 generically as `Control Lines, /CE /OE /LWR /UWR /AS /VRES etc`. To fully
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #emulate a cartridge, you need to map the specific 8 parallel inputs of U6.
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #• Essential Signals (5): `/CE`, `/OE`, `/LWR` (Write Lower), `/UWR` (Write Upper), `/AS`
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #(Address Strobe).
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #• Reset (1): `/VRES` (B27) - Essential for detecting system reset.
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #• Mapper/Compat (1): `/TIME` (B31) - Used for Master System compatibility mode and some
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #mappers.
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #• Spare (1): You have 1 slot left on U6.
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #3. Unaccounted Edge Connector Pins
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #The following pins exist on the physical 64-pin cartridge slot but are not connected in your
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #Netlist. This is likely intentional for a standard ROM cart, but worth noting:
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #• B1 (Audio Left) & B3 (Audio Right): Analog inputs. The cartridge can mix audio into the
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #console's output (e.g., Virtua Racing PWM). Your BOM has no DAC or PWM filtering to drive these.
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #• B2 (/MRES): Master Reset. distinct from `/VRES` (B27). Most carts tie these together or
10aa1c55 [gemini-3-pro] #ignore `/MRES`, relying on `/VRES`.
