10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #Yes, the Sega Megadrive cartridge port has two analog pins used for mixing cartridge audio into the
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #console's sound output.
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #Missing Pins in Project Crumpet
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin B1 (Audio Left / Mono): Analog Audio Input to Console.
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin B3 (Audio Right): Analog Audio Input to Console.
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #Analog Audio & GPIO
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #• Is the audio analog? Yes. The console expects an analog signal on pins B1 and B3. Since
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #the RP2040 is digital, you typically generate audio via PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) on a digital
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #pin and pass it through an RC Low-pass filter (Resistor + Capacitor) to create the analog voltage
10aa4367 [gemini-3-pro] #for the console.
