10aa47cb [gemini-3-pro] #Yes, the Sega Megadrive cartridge slot has two analog audio pins (B1 and B3) which allow the
10aa47cb [gemini-3-pro] #cartridge to mix audio into the console's main output (used by games like Virtua Racing).
10aa47cb [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa47cb [gemini-3-pro] #Missing Pins / Audio Logic
10aa47cb [gemini-3-pro] #• Missing: Pin B1 (Audio Mono/Left) and B3 (Audio Right).
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #• Direction: These are Inputs to the Console, meaning the Cartridge (RP2040) must
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #Output to them if you want to generate sound.
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #• RP2040 Implementation: Since the RP2040 outputs digital, you would typically use
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #PWM on a spare GPIO with an RC filter (Resistor+Capacitor) to create the analog signal sent
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #to B1/B3.
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #Analog Inputs (ADC) on RP2040
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #If you intend to sample signals (e.g. if this is a sniffer rather than a cart emulator),
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #the RP2040 has specific pins for Analog to Digital Conversion (ADC):
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #1.  GP26 (ADC0): Available (Currently `SPARE_0`).
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #2.  GP27 (ADC1): Available (Currently `SPARE_1`).
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #3.  GP28 (ADC2): Occupied. Currently assigned to `MD_CLK`.
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #To use 3 analog inputs, you would need to move `MD_CLK` to a different digital pin (e.g., GP0 or
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #GP1 if UART isn't needed).
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #
10aa47cc [gemini-3-pro] #Clean JS
