10b478d8 [nitro@ryzen5] what voltage are the chips?
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #• toast.md* - 74HC165 at 3V3, 74LVC245 at 3V3. Both are 3.3V logic, so Q7 outputs are
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #already GPIO-safe. The 10K series resistors are for the 5V C64 bus inputs to the shift registers,
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #not the outputs.
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #• crumpet.md* - 74HC165 at 3V3, 74LVC245 at 3V3, but 74LS374 at 5V. The LS374 latches are
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #5V parts driving the Megadrive data bus. GP10-GP17 driving 5V LS374 inputs should be fine (3.3V
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #exceeds TTL threshold), but the BOM inconsistency is the 48x 10K for shift inputs is correct, Q7
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #outputs don't need protection.
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #So the resistor counts are actually correct - I was wrong about missing Q7 resistors since the 165s
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #run at 3V3.
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #• crumpet* issue: 74LS374 is a 5V part being fed by 3.3V GPIO. Works for TTL thresholds but
10b4798a [claude-opus-4-5] #worth noting. Could substitute 74LVC374 for cleaner 3.3V operation.
10b4798b [claude-opus-4-5] #
