10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #Looks good. File matches what we discussed.
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #A few observations:
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #1. GPIO shortage - 4 joysticks × 5 lines = 20 GPIOs for input alone. You're using GP2-GP21
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #which leaves little room for output driving. The CD4066 switches help but need control lines too.
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #2. CD4066 control - Not yet allocated. Need 4 GPIOs minimum to select which input routes to
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #which output.
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #3. Output driving - The 4× DE9 male outputs need GPIO allocation or mux logic.
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #Options:
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #• A) Shift register approach* - Add 74HC165 for reading, 74HC595 for driving outputs. Frees
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #GPIOs for CD4066 control.
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #• B) Reduce scope* - 2 inputs, 2 outputs active at once, directly switched.
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #• C) I2C expander* - MCP23017 gives 16 extra GPIOs.
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #Which direction interests you?
10b8beb0 [claude-opus-4-5] #
