10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #Hi. I have reviewed the Project Joy documentation. There are significant conflicts between
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #the GPIO Allocation section and the Wiring section that need resolution before
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #layout.
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #Critical Issues
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  GPIO Conflict (GP5 - GP9):
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Allocation Section: Lists GP5 as `FET SEL`, and GP6–8 as `MUX S0–S2`.
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Wiring Section: Lists GP5, GP6, GP7, and GP8 as distinct Data Inputs (Q7)
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #for Shift Registers U2, U3, U4, and U5.
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Impact: You cannot drive the Multiplexers/FETs and read separate shift registers on
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #the same pins.
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #
10ba9c17 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Shift Register Topology:
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The wiring currently describes a Parallel configuration (consuming 5 GPIOs for
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #data).
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Recommendation: Use a Daisy Chain configuration. Connect `Q7` of U1 to `DS`
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #(Serial Input) of U2, and so on. This requires only 1 GPIO (GP4) for all 5 shift registers,
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #freeing up GP5–GP8 for the MUX and Select lines.
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Missing Netlist Details:
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   CD4051 Analog Mux: The BOM includes them, and GP26/27 are assigned to ADCs, but the
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #netlist does not define the connections for the Mux Select lines (S0-S2) or the Joystick
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #Potentiometer inputs.
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Sega Select: The "Multiple select cycles" feature requires a dedicated output line
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #to toggle Pin 7 on the Sega ports. This is alluded to as `fet SEL out` on GP5 but needs to be
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #explicit in the netlist.
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Voltage Levels:
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   74HC165 powered at 3.3V reading 5V logic: Ensure the 10kΩ series resistors mentioned in the
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #summary are strictly applied to limit current into the input protection diodes.
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #Suggested Resolution
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #
10ba9c18 [gemini-3-pro] #Switching to a daisy-chain shift register input resolves the pin shortage. Here is a corrected GPIO
