10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #Hi, I have reviewed the WIP documentation for Project Joy.
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is a summary of the issues found in the netlist and logic, specifically regarding the Shift
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #Register chaining and Voltage compliance.
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #1. Shift Register Daisy Chain (Logic Direction)
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #The netlist for the 74HC165 cascade appears to be wired backwards for a standard "Shift In"
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #configuration where `U1` is closest to the RP2040.
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #• Current (Incorrect) logic:*
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #• `U1.9 (Q7)` → `U2.10 (DS)`
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #• `U5.9 (Q7)` → `GND` (Shorting an output to ground)
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #• Correction:*
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #Data must flow towards the Pico. `U1` feeds the Pico, `U2` feeds `U1`, etc. The last chip
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #(`U5`) should have its Serial Input (`DS`) grounded (or tied High), and its Output (`Q7`) feeds the
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #previous chip.
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #Corrected Chain:
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #Pico GP4 (MISO) <── U1.9 (Q7)
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #                    U1.10 (DS) <── U2.9 (Q7)
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #                    U2.10 (DS) <── U3.9 (Q7)
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #                    ...
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #                    U5.10 (DS) <── GND
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #2. Voltage Levels & Protection
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #• 74HC165 Power: You have `VCC` tied to `3V3`.
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #• Input Levels: Vintage joysticks/consoles operate at 5V.
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #• Risk: Feeding 5V signals (from the joystick port) directly into a 74HC165 powered by 3.3V
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #exceeds the input voltage tolerance (V_CC + 0.5V).
10bae3c6 [gemini-3-pro] #• Fix: You need current limiting series resistors (e.g., 1kΩ - 10kΩ) on the joystick inputs
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #(P0-P7) to allow the 74HC165 internal clamping diodes to handle the 5V safely, similar to your
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Toast design.
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #3. Missing Connections
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Sega Select (Multiplexer): `GP5` is allocated as `fet SEL out (Sega)`, but it is not
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #listed in the DB9 header pinouts or the netlist. Sega controllers require this pin (usually DB9 Pin
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #7) to toggle High/Low to read the full 12-button state.
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Analog Mux (CD4051): The BOM lists 2x CD4051, and GPIOs are allocated for `ADC0/1` and
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #`MUX S0-S2`, but the netlist does not define which DB9 pins (Pot X/Y) connect to the Mux inputs
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #(Y0-Y7).
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #4. Apple II Paddle Logic
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #Apple II paddles are variable resistors (0-150kΩ), not voltage dividers.
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #• To read these via ADC, you need a pull-up resistor (e.g., 3.3kΩ to 3.3V) on the Mux Common line
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #or individual inputs to create a voltage divider the ADC can read. The current BOM/Netlist does not
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #show this bias resistor.
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #5. BOM Discrepancies
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Resistors: BOM lists "10x 10kΩ resistor (pull-ups)".
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   With 5 chips x 8 inputs = 40 inputs.
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Atari/C64 joysticks switch to Ground. You need pull-ups on all inputs unless relying on
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #internal MCU/Shift register weak pull-ups (HC165 usually requires external pull-ups or inputs will
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #float). 10 resistors is insufficient for 40 inputs.
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #Summary
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #The project needs a logic reversal on the shift register chain and specific attention to 5V-to-3.3V
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #input protection to avoid damaging the RP2040 or the logic chips.
10bae3c7 [gemini-3-pro] #
