10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #Here is a review of the Project Joy work-in-progress document.
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #Logic and Netlist Review
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #• 1. Analog Multiplexers (Missing Wiring)*
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #The BOM lists 2x CD4051 and GPIOs are allocated for MUX S0-S2 and ADC0/1, but the Wiring
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #section completely omits the CD4051 connections.
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #• You need to map the Joystick Potentiometer pins (DB9 Pin 5 and 9) to the CD4051 inputs (Y0-Y7).
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #• Ensure the Common Output (Z) of the muxes connects to GP26/GP27.
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #• 2. Shift Register Chain*
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #The daisy-chain logic in the final revision is correct for data flowing towards the RP2040:
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #`GND -> U5(DS) -> U5(Q7) -> U4(DS)... -> U1(Q7) -> GP4`
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #• Observation: Ensure U5 Pin 10 is pulled to the logic state you want to shift in when the
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #chain runs out of data (usually logic 0/GND is fine, but strictly defining it prevents floating
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #bits).
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #• 3. Voltage Levels (3.3V vs 5V)*
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #You are powering the 74HC165s with 3V3.
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #• Passive Controllers: Works fine for Atari/C64 (switches to ground).
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #• Active Controllers: Sega Genesis/Megadrive controllers are active 5V devices. Feeding a
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #logic High (5V) into a 74HC165 powered at 3.3V violates Vin \le VCC. This can damage the
10baf40b [gemini-3-pro] #shift registers or the RP2040 via current injection.
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• Fix: Run the 74HC165s at 5V and place a voltage divider (or level shifter) on the
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #final `Q7 -> GP4` line.
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• 4. Sega Select Line*
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• GPIO: GP5 is allocated as `fet SEL out (Sega)`.
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• Wiring: The netlist does not show the connection from GP5 to the DB9 connectors.
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• Requirement: Connect GP5 (likely via a level shifter or open drain FET if the controllers
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #are 5V) to Pin 7 of the Sega input ports to allow multiplexing between D-Pad and Buttons.
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• 5. Latch Mapping (Remote Drive)*
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #The bit-packing across U9, U10, and U11 is efficient but complex:
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• Joy 2 is split between U9 (Q5-Q7) and U10 (Q0-Q1).
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• Joy 4 is split between U10 (Q7) and U11 (Q0-Q3).
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• Ensure your software abstraction layer handles these split masks correctly when writing to the
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #latches.
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #Minor Notes
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• U11 Wiring: The list for U11 stops at Q3. Q4-Q7 should be explicitly marked NC or
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #grounded if unused inputs (though these are outputs on a 374, so NC is fine).
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #• Apple II: U5 inputs P0-P2 are mapped to Apple buttons. Ensure the Apple II joystick
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #connector provides a ground reference compatible with the board.
10baf40c [gemini-3-pro] #
