10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is a review of the Project Joy documentation (specifically the final iteration
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #provided in the text).
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #Logic & Electrical Review
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Shift Register Input Levels (Critical)
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: The netlist powers the 74HC165 chips at 3.3V (`U1.16, VCC, 3V3`).
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Risk: Legacy joysticks (Atari/C64/Sega) typically output 5V logic signals. Feeding
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #5V signals directly into a 74HC165 powered at 3.3V exceeds the absolute maximum input rating (VCC +
10bb0051 [gemini-3-pro] #0.5V) and may damage the chips or the RP2040.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Fix: Use 5V tolerant shift registers (e.g., 74LVC series) or add input voltage
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #dividers similar to Project Fifteen/Toast.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Missing Sega Button Inputs (Regression)
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: In the final "wiring" block, pins U1.3 to U1.6 (P4-P7) are listed as `NC`.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Context: In the first wiring iteration, these were mapped to `Joy1 B`, `Joy1 C`,
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #`Joy1 A`, and `Joy1 Start`.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Fix: Revert U1 connections to include the extra Sega buttons, otherwise only
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #directional inputs are read.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Analog Multiplexer (CD4051) Missing
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: The BOM lists 2x CD4051 and GPIOs 6, 7, 8, 26, and 27 are allocated for MUX
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #control/reading.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Observation: There is no netlist section detailing the wiring of the joystick POT
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #X/Y lines to the CD4051 inputs (Y0-Y7) or the connection to the RP2040.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #4.  GPIO 5 (Sega Select)
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Issue: `GP5` is allocated as "fet SEL out (Sega)" to handle multiplexing for
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #3-button/6-button controllers.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Observation: This connection is missing from the Netlist/Open Drain Drivers
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #section. It needs to drive pin 7 (Select) on the DB9 connectors.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #Documentation Consistency
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #• Duplicate Sections: The provided text contains three slightly different versions of the
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #wiring section for Project Joy. The review assumes the final block is the intended master, but it
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #appears to be the most incomplete regarding button mapping.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #• GPIO 9: Listed as empty in the allocation list.
10bb0052 [gemini-3-pro] #
