10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #Hello, here is a review of the Project Joy documentation.
10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #Overall the logic is sound, but there are significant voltage domain risks regarding the 5V
10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #peripherals interacting with the 3.3V RP2040.
10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #Schematic & Safety Logic
10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #• Input Voltage Mismatch (74HC165): The shift registers are powered by 3V3. If connected to
10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #active joysticks (Sega pads, auto-fire sticks) running on 5V, the logic high input will exceed VCC.
10bb2473 [gemini-3-pro] #       Mitigation:* Ensure the "80x 10kΩ resistors" in the BOM are placed in series
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #with the inputs to limit current through the clamping diodes.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #• ADC Voltage Levels: Joystick potentiometers (IBM/Apple/C64 paddles) act as voltage
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #dividers against their supply rail. If that rail is 5V, the output to the CD4051 → RP2040 ADC will
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #exceed 3.3V.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #       Required:* Voltage dividers on the analog inputs or the multiplexer output.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pin 7 Conflict: The note `Ensure DB9 Pin 7 is switchable` is critical.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #       Sega:* Pin 7 is an Output (Select) from the RP2040.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #       Atari:* Pin 7 is +5V Power input for the joystick.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #       Risk:* Connecting a Sega pad to a port hardwired for Atari +5V will short the Select
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #signal. This requires a physical jumper or FET switch in the netlist.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #Wiring & Netlist Inconsistencies
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #• U5.14 (P3):
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #       In Wiring / Shift In*: Listed as `U5.14, P3, NC`.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #       In Software / Shift Chain*: Listed as `Btn2` (Apple).
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #       Correction:* Connect U5.14 to the Apple II Button 2 header pin.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #• Joy 4 Split:
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Joy 4 is split across U10 (Up) and U11 (Dn, Lt, Rt, Fire).
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   This is electrically fine but requires careful bit-masking in the software driver.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #• Output Drivers (74LS374):
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   These latches actively drive High (Push-Pull).
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   If the target "Remote" console expects Open Collector/Drain signals (pull-to-ground only),
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #driving a hard 3.3V/5V logic High into the console's input matrix may cause contention or ghosting.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #       Comparison:* Project Toast uses 2N7000 FETs (Open Drain), which is safer for vintage
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #bus simulation.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #BOM Notes
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #• Resistor Count: The BOM lists "80x 10kΩ resistor". This implies series protection for all
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #4 ports × 9 pins + Apple lines, which is good practice.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #• Multiplexers: The BOM lists "2x CD4051" but the wiring only details the Select lines
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #(S0-S2). Ensure the Z (Common In/Out) pins map correctly to GP26 and GP27.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #JS Config Update
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #The software config `notes` array should explicitly mention the Joy4 split across latches.
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #module.exports = {
10bb2474 [gemini-3-pro] #	name: "Project Joy",
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #	// ... existing config ...
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #	shift_chain: [
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #		// ... existing chain ...
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #		{
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #			id: "U5",
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #			device: "Apple",
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #			inputs: ["Btn0", "Btn1", "Btn2", "NC", "NC", "NC", "NC", "NC"]
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #		}
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #	],
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #	notes: [
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #		"Ensure DB9 Pin 7 is switchable between +5V (Atari) and GPIO_5 (Sega Select).",
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #		"Joy 4 output is split: 'Up' is on Latch U10 (bit 7), remaining direction/fire on Latch U11."
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #	]
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #};
10bb2475 [gemini-3-pro] #
