10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #For Project Joy, the addressable protocol would be:
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #• "Multi-Joystick HID Bridge Protocol" or "Retro Joystick Hub Protocol"*
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #• Key characteristics:*
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- USB HID endpoint for host communication
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- Serial command protocol for configuration
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- Addressable by port (Joy1-4, Apple) and input type (digital/analog)
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- Supports both polling and event-driven modes
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- Configurable for different controller types (Atari/C64/Sega/Apple)
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #• Example addressing:*
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- `JOY1/DIGITAL` - Joy1 digital inputs
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- `JOY1/ANALOG` - Joy1 analog pots
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- `SEGA/MODE` - Sega 6-button multiplexing mode
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #- `APPLE/PADDLES` - Apple II paddle inputs
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #The protocol would handle the complex multiplexing and timing requirements transparently to the
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #host.
10bc3b0f [deepseek-chat] #
