10bc5e92 [nitro@ryzen5] The Apple 2 pinout, as csv plase
10bc61e8 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the information on the addressable LEDs, the Apple II pinouts, and the utilization of the
10bc61e8 [gemini-3-pro] #remaining latch pins.
10bc61e8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc61e8 [gemini-3-pro] #WS2812B
10bc61e8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Protocol Name: Single-wire NRZ (Non-Return-to-Zero) asynchronous serial. Often referred
10bc61e8 [gemini-3-pro] #to generically as "NeoPixel" (Adafruit trade name) or "Addressable LED".
10bc61e8 [gemini-3-pro] #• What is B: The 'B' stands for the specific package revision.
10bc61e8 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   WS2812: Original 6-pin component.
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   WS2812B: Improved 4-pin component (integrated protection, better brightness,
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #separate power/control layout not required).
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #RP2040 SEL Button
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #The BOOTSEL button on the Pico can be used as a user input, but it is not a standard GPIO.
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #Reading it requires the code to briefly disable interrupts and talk to the flash memory chip (CS
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #pin), which can cause glitches in timing-critical applications (like bit-banging video or
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #high-speed serial).
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #• Verdict: Good for "Mode Select" or "Setup" at startup. Bad for "Fire Button" during
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #gameplay.
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #U8 Latch & Apple II "Resonators"
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #You are likely thinking of Annunciators.
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #• Annunciators (AN0-AN3): These are digital Outputs from the Apple II (used
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #to turn on stepper motors or switch banks). Since U8 is an output from the RP2040, you
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #cannot drive the Apple's outputs.
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #• Buttons (SW0-SW2): These are digital Inputs to the Apple II.
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #• Utilization: Yes, you can use U8 Q4 and U8 Q5 to drive Apple II
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #SW0 and SW1. This allows the RP2040 to "press the buttons" on the Apple II.
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #Apple II Game Port Pinouts
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the CSV data for the internal DIP16 socket (Logic Board) and the external DB9 connector
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #(Apple //e, //c, IIGS).
10bc61e9 [gemini-3-pro] #
