10bc77e1 [nitro@ryzen5] 4 more analog ins, any ideas?
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #The "Apple resonators" are the Annunciators (AN0-AN3). These are digital outputs from an
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #Apple II normally used to switch stepper motors (in disk drives) or handle special joystick
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #features. If we are the host, we can drive them to support complex controllers.
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #To get 4 more analog inputs, we can utilize the unused channels on the second CD4051 (U10).
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #It only uses 4 channels for the Apple paddles, leaving 4 spare.
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the updated configuration.
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #Project Joy
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #
10bc7cc3 [gemini-3-pro] #RP2040 multi-joystick hub with ribbon breakouts.
