10bcc3e6 [nitro@ryzen5] Shared OE means data always latched, latches pull low or float.
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #The 'B' in WS2812B indicates the updated silicon revision (Generation B). It improved on
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #the original WS2812 by reducing the pin count from 6 to 4 (integrating power/ground) and adding
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #reverse polarity protection and better brightness consistency.
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the finalized specification for Project Joy.
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #• Apple II Outputs: Mapped the "Resonators" (Annunciators) to the spare bits on the third
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #latch (U8).
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #• Spare Analog: The 4 remaining channels on the second multiplexer (U10) are broken out to
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #an auxiliary header.
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #• GP22: Assigned to Apple Strobe, a dedicated signal often used for latching data
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #on the Apple game port.
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #• Output Enable: Tied `GP21` to `/OE`. While 74LS374s are totem-pole (push-pull), driving a
10bcc8fd [gemini-3-pro] #Logic 1 (5V) into a pulled-up console input is standard practice. To "float" the bus completely,
10bcc8fe [gemini-3-pro] #toggle GP21 High.
10bcc8fe [gemini-3-pro] #
10bcc8fe [gemini-3-pro] #Project Joy
10bcc8fe [gemini-3-pro] #
10bcc8fe [gemini-3-pro] #An RP2040 multi-joystick hub. Reads standard DB9 controllers and drives vintage computer ports via
10bcc8fe [gemini-3-pro] #DE9 cables.
