10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #No, none of those are open-drain latches.
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #The 74HC374 and 74HC573 are both totem-pole output latches - they actively drive high or low.
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #For true open-drain you'd need:
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #- ULN2803 - 8-channel Darlington (sinks only, needs external pull-up)
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #- 74HC05 - Hex inverter, open-drain
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #- 74HC03 - Quad NAND, open-drain
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #Alternatively, keep 74HC374 ($1.59) and add 8× 2N7000 per latch for open-drain conversion. That's
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #the pattern used in your other designs.
10bcda6c [claude-opus-4-5] #
10bcda6d [claude-opus-4-5] #Or reconsider the requirement - if driving active-low joystick lines that expect passive-high, the
10bcda6d [claude-opus-4-5] #74HC374 with active-low logic might suffice if the target has internal pull-ups.
10bcda6d [claude-opus-4-5] #
