10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #2N7000, and WS2812B support.
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #  - BOM and GPIO layout are explicit and show 5V-to-3.3V considerations.
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #- node.md
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #  - New: “cbm node” concept (RP2040 + C64 user port) with 2x74HC165, 1x74LVC245, 6x 2N7000, shift
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #and latch details, plus a JSON-style software link snippet.
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #- crumpet.md
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #  - New: Megadrive cartridge interface using 64-pin edge, 4x74HC165, 2x74LVC245, 2x74LS374,
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #2x2N7000, detailed shift/latch wiring.
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #  - Comprehensive GPIO/netlist staging for the cart signals.
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #- toast.md (already noted) and Crumpet together imply a family of designs using universal patterns:
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #shift registers for input, latches for output, open-drain FETs for active-low signals, and careful
10bd69a9 [gpt-5-nano] #voltage-level considerations.
10bd69aa [gpt-5-nano] #
10bd69aa [gpt-5-nano] #- designs.md
