10be2da1 [gemini-3-pro] #Based on the pinout and component specifications, here is the summary of PIO steps required to
10be2da1 [gemini-3-pro] #handle the inputs and outputs.
10be2da1 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be2da1 [gemini-3-pro] #Input PIO Strategy (74HC165 Shift Chain)
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #• Goal:* Read 40 bits of data (5 chips × 8 bits) from `SHIFTDATAIN` (GP4).
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Pin Configuration: Map `SHIFTCLK` (GP2) as a side-set pin, `SHIFTSHLD`
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #(GP3) as a set pin, and `SHIFTDATA_IN` (GP4) as the input source.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Latch Step: Drive `SHIFTSHLD` low for one cycle, then high. This captures the
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #parallel state of the buttons into the shift registers.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Shift Loop: Enter a loop to read the data stream.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Read the state of `SHIFTDATAIN` using the `in` instruction.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Toggle `SHIFT_CLK` high then low using side-set to shift the next bit into position.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Push: Enable auto-push on the State Machine (e.g., every 8 or 32 bits) to send the
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #collected button states to the main processor via the RX FIFO.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #Output PIO Strategy (74LS374 Latch Array)
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #• Goal:* Drive 24 bits of data to 3 latches using a shared 8-bit bus (GP10-GP17) and
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #individual clocks (GP18-GP20).
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Pin Configuration: Map GP10-GP17 as the `out` pin group (Data Bus). Map GP18 (CP0),
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #GP19 (CP1), and GP20 (CP2) as `set` or `side-set` pins.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Data Formatting: The main CPU packs the 24 bits of FET state data into a single 32-bit
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #word and pushes it to the TX FIFO.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Latch 1 (Joy 1+2):
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Pull 8 bits from the FIFO to the Output pins (GP10-GP17).
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Pulse `LATCH_CP0` (GP18) high then low to lock the data into U6.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Latch 2 (Joy 2+3+4):
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Pull the next 8 bits from the FIFO to the Output pins.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Pulse `LATCH_CP1` (GP19) high then low to lock the data into U7.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #5.  Latch 3 (Joy 4 + Apple):
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Pull the final 8 bits from the FIFO to the Output pins.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Pulse `LATCH_CP2` (GP20) high then low to lock the data into U8.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #6.  Repeat: The PIO program wraps back to the start, waiting for the next data update from
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #the CPU.
10be2da2 [gemini-3-pro] #
