10be90ff [gemini-3-pro] #Thank you for the detailed update. The specifications for the Vintage Kid suite are
10be90ff [gemini-3-pro] #comprehensive.
10be90ff [gemini-3-pro] #
10be90ff [gemini-3-pro] #Here are observations regarding the new BOM details and technical consistency across the designs:
10be90ff [gemini-3-pro] #
10be90ff [gemini-3-pro] #1. Component Selection & Logic Levels
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #• 74HC165 (Shift Inputs): You are powering these at 3.3V.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Crumpet/Toast: You specified 10kΩ series resistors. This is the correct
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #value to limit current through the clamping diodes when interfacing 5V targets.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Node: You specified 1kΩ series resistors. Recommendation: Increase
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #"Node" resistors to 10kΩ to match Crumpet/Toast. 1kΩ allows ~1.7mA through the clamp diodes
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #(5V - 3.3V / 1000), which is safe but higher than necessary. 10kΩ reduces this to ~0.17mA.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #• 74LS374 (Latches): You have selected LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   These run on 5V. The RP2040 (3.3V) can reliably drive LS TTL inputs (V_IH = 2.0V).
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Note: LS parts consume significantly more static power than CMOS (HC/HCT). Ensure
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #your power budget (USB or external) can handle the quiescent current of multiple LS chips, though
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #for mains-powered retro consoles this is rarely an issue.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #2. Project Crumpet (Megadrive)
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #• Timing Constraint: The architecture uses shift registers to read the Address Bus
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #(A1-A23).
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Observation: Serializing a 23-bit address read via PIO takes significant clock
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #cycles compared to the Megadrive's access window (~150ns-250ns).
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Implication: This design is excellent for a Cartridge Dumper/Writer or
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #save-game manager. However, it may be too slow to act as a real-time Flash Cart (ROM emulator) for
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #playing games, as the RP2040 cannot shift address in, fetch data, and latch data out fast enough
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #for the 68000 bus cycle.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #3. Project Joy
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #• Sega Mux: The logic correctly handles the specific multiplexing required for Sega
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #3-button and 6-button controllers using the `SEGA_SEL` line.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #• Protection: The use of 10kΩ series resistors on the 74HC165 inputs is crucial here, as
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #vintage controllers often short lines directly to 5V.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #4. Project LUMA2
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #• Comparators: The switch to LM319 is noted. This is a high-speed comparator (80ns
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #response), which is suitable for the pixel clock of the C64.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #• Grey Levels: With 3 comparators for luma (plus sync), you can detect 4 states (Sync,
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #Dark, Mid, Light). To get full 2-bit luma (Black, Dark Grey, Light Grey, White), the threshold
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #tuning via the Piher trimpots will be critical.
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be9100 [gemini-3-pro] #5. BOM & Sourcing
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #• The Jaycar parts listed are standard through-hole components, making assembly accessible.
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #• 2N7000: Excellent choice for the "Open Drain" simulation on the C64/Amiga control lines
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #(/IRQ, /NMI, /DTACK). This prevents bus contention voltage spikes.
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #Summary of Changes
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #The primary new content is the specific Jaycar BOM integration and the finalized
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #GPIO/Netlist for Project Node. The logic remains consistent with previous iterations, with
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #the specific refinement of using 74LVC245 for high-speed output buffering and 74HC165/Resistors for
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #input protection.
10be9101 [gemini-3-pro] #
