10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the assessment for adding the LCD and Stereo Audio to Luma2, along with an
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #explanation of IPS and the Chroma strategy.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #1. What is IPS?
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• IPS (In-Plane Switching)* is a screen technology used in modern LCDs.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Viewing Angles: You can look at the screen from the side, up, or down, and the colors do
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #not invert or wash out (unlike older TN screens).
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Color: It produces much more vibrant and accurate colors.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Relevance: For a retro project, IPS is highly recommended because it mimics the vibrancy
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #of a CRT better than cheap TN panels.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #2. Chroma: Edge Counting vs. More Bits
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #For the C64, Edge Counting via PIO is likely the best approach for this specific hardware.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• How it works: The PIO measures the time distance between the Horizontal Sync and the
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #zero-crossing of the Chroma signal. This determines the phase, which determines the color.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Is it enough? Yes. The C64 only has 16 colors. The phase differences between them are
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #significant enough that a fast PIO counter (~125MHz or overclocked) can distinguish them.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• More Comparators? Adding more comparators (flash ADC style) adds significant component
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #cost and complexity for diminishing returns on an RP2040. The bottleneck is usually the timing
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #resolution of the capture, not the voltage levels, since Chroma is phase-modulated.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #3. GPIO Audit & LCD Selection
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• Waveshare 1.14" vs 2.0":*
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• 1.14" (240x135): Too small. You would have to crop or scale down the C64's 320x200 image,
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #losing detail.
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #• 2.0" IPS (320x240): Perfect fit. You can display the full 320x200 C64 image with
10c07be7 [gemini-3-pro] #a small border for status/UI.
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #• GPIO Availability:*
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Current Luma2: Uses ~7 pins.
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Stereo Audio: Uses 2 pins (ADC).
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #• SPI LCD: Uses ~5-6 pins.
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Total: ~15 pins used.
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pico Capacity: 26 GPIO available. Status: PLENTY of room.
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #Pinout Re-Shuffle
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Critical Note:* Most Pico LCD "Hats" hardwire the screen to specific pins (usually SPI0 on
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #GP16-GP20). Your current Luma2 design uses GP16-GP22 for video input.
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Action: Move Luma2 video inputs to GP0-GP6* to leave the standard SPI pins free
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #for the LCD.
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #Updated Project Luma2 Spec
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #Includes Stereo Audio, 2.0" IPS LCD support, and re-mapped GPIO to avoid SPI conflicts.
10c07be8 [gemini-3-pro] #
