10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #The Nintendo Game Boy Advance cartridge connector has 32 pins (16 pins per side).
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #GBA Cartridge Pinout Summary:
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #- 32 total pins (2.54mm/0.1" pitch)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #- 16 pins per side (edge connector)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #- 3.3V logic levels (compatible with RP2040 directly)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #- 5V tolerant I/O on some pins (for legacy GB/GBC games)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #Key Signal Groups:
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #1. Address Bus: A0-A15 (16-bit, 64KB banked addressing)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #2. Data Bus: D0-D7 (8-bit)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #3. Control Signals: /RD, /WR, /CS, /RESET
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #4. Bank Switching: A16-A23 (via GPIO or latch)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #5. Save Memory: /CS2, various control lines for SRAM/Flash/EEPROM
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #For Your Waffle Design:
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #- Direct 3.3V compatibility simplifies design (no level shifters needed)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #- Need to handle wait state timing (GBA has strict access timing)
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #- Bank switching required for >64KB ROMs
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #- Save memory support adds complexity
10ca0e2e [deepseek-chat] #
10ca0e2f [deepseek-chat] #The 32-pin count makes it one of your simpler physical interfaces (compared to 64-pin Megadrive or
10ca0e2f [deepseek-chat] #44-pin C64).
