10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #Based on the provided files, here is an analysis of the pin mapping between the RP2040 and the GBA
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #Cartridge port.
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #Hardware Architecture Analysis
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #The GPIO allocation suggests the RP2040 is acting as a GBA Cartridge Emulator (Flashcart)
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #rather than a dumper/writer.
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Address/Data Bus (AD0-AD15): The multiplexed low address and data lines are mapped
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #contiguously to GP7–GP22. This is ideal for RP2040 PIO (Programmable I/O) state machines to
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #handle the bus timing efficiently.
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Upper Address Lines (A16-A23): There are no direct GPIOs assigned to GBA pins 22–29
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #(A16–A23).
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The presence of GP2 (SHIFTCLK), GP3 (SHIFTSHLD), and GP4
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #(SHIFTQ7) strongly implies a 74HC165 PISO (Parallel-In Serial-Out) shift register
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #is used.
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The GBA drives A16–A23 into the shift register, and the RP2040 reads the address serially
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #via GP4.
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Control Signals: All critical control lines (/CS, /RD, /WR, PHI, /CS2) are mapped
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #directly.
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #Combined Pin Mapping
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the correlation between the provided CSV pinout and the RP2040 GPIO list:
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #╭──────────────────┬───────────┬──────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────╮
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #│  Signal Name     │  GBA Pin  │  RP2040 GPIO     │  Function                            │
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #├──────────────────┼───────────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #│  :---            │  :---     │  :---            │  :---                                │
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #│  **VCC**         │  1, 32    │  N/A             │  3.3V Power                          │
10cb6efd [gemini-3-pro] #│  **PHI**         │  2        │  **GP28**        │  System Clock (~16.78MHz)            │
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #│  **/WR**         │  3        │  **GP27**        │  Write Strobe                        │
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #│  **/RD**         │  4        │  **GP26**        │  Read Strobe                         │
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #│  **/CS**         │  5        │  **GP5**         │  ROM Chip Select                     │
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #│  **AD0 – AD15**  │  6 – 21   │  **GP7 – GP22**  │  Multiplexed Address/Data            │
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #│  **A16 – A23**   │  22 – 29  │  *Indirect*      │  Via Shift Register (GP2, GP3, GP4)  │
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #│  **/CS2**        │  30       │  **GP6**         │  SRAM/Save Chip Select               │
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #│  **GND**         │  31       │  N/A             │  Ground                              │
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #╰──────────────────┴───────────┴──────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────╯
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #Implementation Notes
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #• Contiguous GPIOs: GP7 through GP22 form a perfect 16-bit block. In C/C++ SDK, this allows
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #a single `gpiogetall()` masked operation or a `in` instruction in PIO to capture the entire
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #bus instantly.
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #• Shift Register Timing: Since the GBA access time is fast, the PIO code will likely need
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #to trigger the `SHIFTSHLD` immediately upon detecting a valid address setup to capture
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #A16-A23 before the GBA bus cycle completes.
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #• UART: GP0/GP1 are reserved for debugging, which is standard practice.
10cb6efe [gemini-3-pro] #
