10cb8619 [gemini-3-pro] #Yes, the PCB for a Game Boy Advance cartridge is significantly thinner than the standard 1.6mm used
10cb8619 [gemini-3-pro] #in most electronics. Using a standard thickness board will damage the pins in the GBA cartridge
10cb8619 [gemini-3-pro] #slot.
10cb8619 [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb8619 [gemini-3-pro] #Here are the standard dimensions for a GBA cartridge PCB:
10cb8619 [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb8619 [gemini-3-pro] #• Thickness*
10cb8619 [gemini-3-pro] #• 0.8 mm (Critical)
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #• Note: Standard FR4 is usually 1.6mm. You must specify 0.8mm to your fabrication house.
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #• Dimensions (Approximate)*
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #• Width: 54.5 mm (fits inside the standard shell)
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #• Height: 34.5 mm (standard ROM cart size)
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #• Notches: There are specific cutouts required on the sides to fit the plastic posts inside
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #the cartridge shell.
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #• Fabrication Recommendations*
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Edge Connector: Hard Gold plating (ENIG is acceptable for prototypes, but wears out
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #faster).
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Edge Beveling (Chamfer): Highly recommended (usually 30° or 45°) to ensure the 0.8mm
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #board slides into the connector smoothly without catching pins.
10cb861a [gemini-3-pro] #
