10ced03f [nitro@ryzen5] how does kicad colorise its step files, or does it use the older file format
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #KiCad uses the STEP AP214 protocol for colorizing models. It does not rely on an external
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #palette like CGA, nor does it default to the older VRML (.wrl) format for color unless specifically
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #configured to do so.
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #You should avoid a CGA palette; it is too limited for PCB rendering (which requires specific shades
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #for resins, metals, and silkscreens). Instead, you should extract the RGB values directly from the
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #STEP entities.
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #To extract materials from a STEP file, you need to follow a chain of entity references. The
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #geometry (like `MANIFOLDSOLIDBREP`) is linked to color definitions via `STYLED_ITEM`.
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the typical entity chain you need to parse to find the color of a shape:
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #1.  `STYLED_ITEM`: Links a geometric representation (the item) to a style.
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #2.  `PRESENTATIONSTYLEASSIGNMENT`: Referenced by the styled item.
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #3.  `SURFACESTYLEUSAGE`: Defines how the style is applied to the surface.
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #4.  `SURFACESIDESTYLE` & `SURFACESTYLEFILL_AREA`: Defines the
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #visual properties.
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #5.  `COLOUR_RGB`: Contains the actual Red, Green, and Blue values (usually 0.0 to 1.0).
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #I can provide a named function to traverse these relationships and extract colors if you would
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #like.
10ced17f [gemini-3-pro] #
