10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #Regarding the CGA Palette
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #You should not use the CGA palette. STEP files (specifically AP214, which KiCad uses)
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #contain explicit high-fidelity RGB definitions. KiCad exports the specific hex values defined in
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #the footprint properties (e.g., the beige of a plastic connector or the gold of a pin). Using a
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #fixed palette would lose that visual data.
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #How KiCad Colorizes STEP Files
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #KiCad uses the ISO 10303-21 (AP214) protocol for styling. It does not rely on the older
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #VRML sidecar files when you are processing the raw STEP export.
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #The coloring mechanism is a relational chain:
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #1.  `COLOUR_RGB`: Defines the actual Red, Green, Blue values (usually floats between 0.0
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #and 1.0).
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #2.  `FILLAREASTYLECOLOUR` or `SURFACESIDE_STYLE`: Wraps the color.
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #3.  `PRESENTATIONSTYLEASSIGNMENT`: Groups the styles.
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #4.  `STYLEDITEM`: The bridge entity you found in your logs. It assigns the
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #`PRESENTATIONSTYLE` to a specific Geometric Representation Item (the shape).
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #Analyzing Your Log Snippet
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #Your log entries confirm the structure:
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #`#15169 STYLED_ITEM: 'color',(#15170),#8224`
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #• `#15169`: The ID of this assignment.
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #• `'color'`: A generic label.
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #• `(#15170)`: The Style ID. You must look up this entity to find the color chain
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #eventually leading to `COLOUR_RGB`.
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #• `#8224`: The Target Geometry ID. This is the `MANIFOLDSOLIDBREP` or
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #`SHELL` that needs to be painted.
10cedd5b [gemini-3-pro] #
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #Strategy for the Next Step
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #To implement this, you shouldn't just log them; you need to map them.
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Parse Phase: When parsing the file, store entities in a Map for O(1) lookup.
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Color Resolution: Iterate over all `STYLED_ITEM`s.
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Recursively resolve the Style ID (e.g., `#15170`) until you find the RGB values.
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Store the RGB values associated with the Target ID (e.g., `#8224`).
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Mesh Generation: When you tesselate (convert shapes to triangles), check if the shape
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #ID has an assigned color.
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #       Note for glTF:* A single glTF `primitive` can only have one material. You will
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #likely need to group your triangles by color/material when generating the mesh arrays.
10cedd5c [gemini-3-pro] #
