10d02a30 [claude-opus-4-5] #Content noted. The project files describe a coherent RP2040-based retro computing hardware
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #ecosystem:
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #- crumpet: Megadrive 64-pin cart, 6×74HC165 + 2×74LVC245 + 2×74LS374
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #- toast: C64 44-pin expansion, 4×74HC165 + 1×74LVC245 + 7×2N7000
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #- muffin: GBA 32-pin cart, direct 3.3V connection + 1×74HC165 for upper address
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #- fifteen: Multi-port bridge (IEC/GBA link/MD EXT), point-to-point wiring
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #- luma2: Video capture via LM319 comparators, optional display module
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #The GPIO allocations and netlists are well structured. The shift register approach for reading 5V
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #buses through 10kΩ series resistors is sensible, as is the 2N7000 open-drain strategy for driving
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #active-low signals.
10d02a31 [claude-opus-4-5] #
