10d04e4b [nitro@ryzen5] does my megadrive have component? it is original pal with big din connector for video
10d04ed9 [kimi-k2-0905] #The original PAL Mega Drive (and Genesis) only outputs composite video and RGB on the big
10d04ed9 [kimi-k2-0905] #9-pin mini-DIN; there is no native Y-Pb-Pr (component) signal.
10d04ed9 [kimi-k2-0905] #If you want component you’d need an external RGB→YPbPr transcoder, but for Luma2 you can simply tap
10d04ed9 [kimi-k2-0905] #the composite video pin (pin 1) and, if you fit the chroma mod, also grab the clean composite burst
10d04ed9 [kimi-k2-0905] #for the comparator edge-counting.
10d04ed9 [kimi-k2-0905] #
