10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is a review of the two Luma2 SKUs.
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #Verdict: The µ1701-2 (2-inch) is the winner.
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #• Reasoning:*
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  GPIO Compatibility: The 2.8" Touch version is technically incompatible with your
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #current netlist without major rewiring. The Waveshare 2.8" shield hardwires the LCD control and
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #Touch interface to GP16 through GP22. These are the exact pins you have allocated for the
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #Luma2 capture logic (Chroma and Grey levels).
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Aesthetics: The 2" screen has a higher pixel density. For a "Mini Commodore 1701"
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #replica, the smaller screen looks more like a sharp CRT monitor relative to the bezel size. The 4
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #physical buttons on the 2" unit are also perfect for adjusting contrast/brightness without needing
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #a touch driver.
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #Technical Analysis
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #Option A: µ1701-2 (2-inch) - RECOMMENDED
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #This "Hat" fits your GPIO allocation perfectly, provided you use the default Waveshare button
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #mappings (which differ slightly from your text list, but fit the holes in your logic).
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #• LCD SPI: GP8, GP9, GP10, GP11, GP12, GP13 (Matches your allocation).
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #• Physical Buttons: GP2, GP3, GP15, GP17 (Standard Waveshare 2" pinout).
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #• Conflict Check:
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   GP14 (CSYNC) is FREE.
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   GP16 (Chroma) is FREE.
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   GP18-22 (Grey Levels) are FREE.
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #• Form Factor: 40mm width allows for a compact "Monitor" casing with the trimmers mounted
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #on the base PCB below the screen ("Chin" of the monitor).
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #Option B: µ1701-2.8 (2.8-inch Touch) - NOT RECOMMENDED
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #• Conflict: Uses GP16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22 for SPI and Touch.
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #• Result: You would lose your Chroma input and all Grey level inputs. You would have to
10d15659 [gemini-3-pro] #bit-bang SPI on lower pins or cut traces on the LCD PCB.
10d1565a [gemini-3-pro] #
