10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #Design Note: The "Monitor" Look
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #To achieve the "Pots at front, connectors at back" layout with the 2" Hat:
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #1.  PCB Layout: The main Luma2 PCB should be longer than the Pico.
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Mounting:
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Rear: RCA and Power jacks.
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Middle: Socket for the Pico.
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Front: The 5 Piher trimpots arranged in a row (Brightness, Contrast, Saturation,
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #etc.).
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #3.  The Stack: The Pico plugs into the Luma2 PCB. The LCD Hat plugs into the top of the
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #Pico.
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #4.  Case: The 3D print can bezel the screen and the buttons, leaving the trimpots
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #accessible on the "shelf" below the screen, mimicking the control door of a 1701.
10d1565b [gemini-3-pro] #
