10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #Here is the feasibility check and specification update for the Twin 1541 housing, likely
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #intended for the Project Fifteen (IEC Serial) electronics.
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #Enclosure: Twin 1541 (Project Fifteen)
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Concept:* A single housing molded to look like two stacked Commodore 1541 drives.
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #Dimensions (2:13 Scale)
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Width: 32 mm
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Height: 32 mm (16 mm per "drive")
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Depth: 80 mm
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #• Form Factor: Tower
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #Feasibility & Conflicts
10d33af8 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #1.  DIN Connector Clearance (Critical):
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Standard DIN 45322 panel sockets often have a flange diameter of ~15-16mm.
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   With a total height of 32mm (16mm per drive), two standard panel-mount DINs stacked
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #vertically will touch or overlap flanges.
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Solution A: Use PCB-mount DIN sockets (no flange) and have the case act as the
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #faceplate.
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Solution B: Increase height to 34mm (17mm per drive) to allow a 2mm plastic
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #bridge between sockets.
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #2.  PCB Orientation:
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   A 32mm width accommodates the Raspberry Pi Pico (21mm wide) comfortably.
10d33af9 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Recommendation: Mount the PCB vertically (on edge) inside the tower. This allows
