10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #The 2" LCD SKU (1701-2:13) is clear and the pinout looks solid for the Luma2 logic. The
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #move to a "Twin 1541" form factor (32x32x80mm) is a smart play for Project Fifteen/Node to
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #accommodate the bulky DIN connectors, which would never fit in a strict 2:13 scale drive (15mm
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #height).
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #Here are the conflicts and constraints located in the current specs:
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #1. Fatal Conflict: Luma2 vs. Waveshare 2.8" LCD
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #While the 2" LCD works perfectly, the Waveshare 2.8" (µ1701-2.8) listed as an alternative
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #is electrically incompatible with your Luma2 netlist.
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Conflict: The 2.8" Touch version consumes GP16, GP18, GP19, GP20, GP21, GP22 for
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #the display interface and touch controller.
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Impact: These are the exact pins assigned to your Chroma Input (GP16) and
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #Comparator Inputs G0-G4 (GP18-22).
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Resolution: You must strictly stick to the 2" version (or the non-touch 1.3"/1.14"
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #variants) to keep those high-number GPIOs free for the LM319 inputs.
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #2. Mechanical Constraint: 1701-2:13 Case Width
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Case Width: 57.4 mm
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Pico LCD 2 PCB Width: 56.5 mm
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Clearance: 0.9 mm total (0.45 mm per side).
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Note: This is extremely tight. If the 3D print shrinks or corners are rounded, the LCD
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #PCB might not seat flush. Consider widening the case scale slightly to 58-59mm or planning for
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #sanding.
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #3. Mechanical Constraint: Twin 1541 Faceplate (32x32mm)
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Constraint: Standard panel-mount DIN-6 connectors (DIN 45322) often have a face flange
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #diameter of ~19mm.
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Issue: Stacking two DINs vertically in a 32mm high case is physically impossible with
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #standard flanges (19 + 19 = 38mm).
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Resolution:
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Mount them side-by-side? (19 + 19 = 38mm) -> Too wide for 32mm.
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Use PCB-mount DIN sockets without the front flange and recess them inside the case
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #(Body diameter ~14mm; 14+14 = 28mm). This fits within the 32x32mm face.
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #4. Minor GPIO Note: Luma2 Button Inputs
10d34043 [gemini-3-pro] #• Current: `GP2, GP3, GP15, GP17` are defined as inputs for buttons.
10d34044 [gemini-3-pro] #• Check: Ensure internal Pull-Ups are enabled in software, as the Waveshare schematic
10d34044 [gemini-3-pro] #usually grounds the pin on button press. (Standard practice, just a reminder).
10d34044 [gemini-3-pro] #
10d34044 [gemini-3-pro] #Summary
10d34044 [gemini-3-pro] #The 2" LCD is the only viable option for the Luma2 functionality as specified. The Twin
10d34044 [gemini-3-pro] #1541 dimensions are viable only if you use flange-less/internal DIN connectors.
10d34044 [gemini-3-pro] #
