10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #Design Notes & Conflict Check
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #1.  Project Fifteen Physical Constraints:
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The PCB width of 28mm is sufficient for a standard Raspberry Pi Pico (21mm) or
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #RP2040-Zero.
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The DIN-6 connector has a diameter of ~16mm, fitting comfortably within the 28mm
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #width.
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   The case depth was increased to 80mm (vs 62mm scale) to accommodate the inline
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #arrangement of DIN socket + Pico + Headers.
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #2.  Pin Usage:
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Project Fifteen: Uses GP26 (ADC0) as a digital input for Megadrive C/Start. Ensure
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #software disables ADC function on this pin to use digital input buffer.
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Project LUMA2: Uses GP2 and GP3 for LCD Buttons. In Project Fifteen, GP2/3 are IEC
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #signals. This is not a conflict as they are separate devices, but precludes combining
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #codebases without modification.
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #3.  Power:
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Both projects rely on USB power (VBUS).
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Project Fifteen: 5V from VBUS is required for the DIN connector (IEC bus is 5V
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #TTL). The 3.3V logic is handled via the dividers (input) and Open Drain FETs (output).
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #    *   Project LUMA2: LM319 requires 5V (single supply mode supported).
10d3d21a [gemini-3-pro] #
