10d569c0 [nitro@ryzen5] the header24 expansion on the vic:6 what can we add to complete it?
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #Based on the VIC-20's 24-pin expansion port (standard pinout: A0-A13, D0-D7, /RESET, /IRQ, /NMI,
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #/BLK1-5, +5V, GND, etc.), to complete the header24 expansion for VIC:6, consider adding:
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #- Shift Registers: 3x 74HC165 for parallel bus reads (address/data/controls), similar to
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #Toast/Crumpet.
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #- Buffers: 1x 74LVC245 for 8-bit data writes to VIC-20.
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #- Open Drain Drivers: 4x 2N7000 FETs for active-low signals like /RESET, /IRQ, /NMI.
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #- Series Resistors: 10kΩ on all 5V inputs for protection.
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #- Decoupling Caps: 100nF per IC.
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #- GPIO Allocation: Map ~20 GPIOs for bus access, clocks, and controls, leaving room for
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #UART/debug.
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #
10d56a16 [grok-code-1] #This mirrors your other designs for full bus interfacing. PCB size: ~40x25mm at 1:6 scale. If you
