10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #Looking at joy.md - this is a solid multi-joystick design with clever use of 74LS374 latches
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #driving 2N7000 FETs for open-drain outputs. The 40-bit shift chain for inputs and 24-bit latch
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #array for outputs should handle Atari/Commodore/Sega protocols well.
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #A few observations:
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #- The Sega 6-button mapping looks correct (pins 1-4 + 6 for XYZ/ABC)
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #- Analog multiplexing with CD4051s is efficient for paddles
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #- The shared 8-bit data bus for latches reduces GPIO count nicely
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #- Consider adding 100nF caps on each 74LS374 for decoupling
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #- The Apple II DIP-16 connector is a nice touch for full compatibility
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #The PIO strategies look sound - parallel load then shift for inputs, and sequential latch pulses
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #for outputs. Should work well for real-time joystick polling.
10d6092e [kimi-k2-0905] #
