10d60f28 [kimi-k2-0905] #The PCB dimensions in joy.md show 60 × 30 mm (1:6 scale breadbin).
10d60f28 [kimi-k2-0905] #With two DB-9s edge-mounted on the 60 mm side you already consume ~30 mm width, leaving ~25 mm
10d60f28 [kimi-k2-0905] #clear between them.
10d60f28 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d60f28 [kimi-k2-0905] #Quick component tally:
10d60f28 [kimi-k2-0905] #- 5 × 16-pin DIP (74HC165 + 74LS374) ≈ 5 × 8 mm = 40 mm if stacked end-to-end
10d60f28 [kimi-k2-0905] #- 2 × 16-pin SOIC/CD4051 ≈ 6 mm
10d60f28 [kimi-k2-0905] #- 24 × SOT-23 2N7000 ≈ 12 mm × 6 mm cluster
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #- passives 0603 negligible
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #All parts fit comfortably on a single 2-layer board if you:
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. Place the shift/latch chips across the 30 mm depth, perpendicular to the DB-9s.
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. Put the 2N7000 array as a tight grid between the jacks.
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. Route the shared 8-bit bus on the back side—no need for extra layers.
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #You still have room along the 30 mm edge for the 24-pin header24 expansion strip (2 × 12 pins on
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #0.1″ centres = 30.48 mm, exactly the board width).
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #No size changes required; everything packs in with a few mm to spare.
10d60f29 [kimi-k2-0905] #
