10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #Using the CD4051 analog multiplexer for stereo microphone sampling is possible, but
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #with caveats:
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #⚠️ Limitations of CD4051 for Audio
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. Bandwidth: CD4051 is audio-capable but only ~40 kHz @ 5 V (less at 3.3
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #V).
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Acceptable for voice or low-fidelity sampling (8–16 kHz).
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Not hi-fi—roll-off above 5–7 kHz.
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. On-resistance: ~120 Ω typical (5 V).
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Forms a low-pass filter with ADC input capacitance (≈ 12 pF).
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Fc ≈ 110 kHz—fine for 48 kHz sampling, but SNR degrades.
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. Crosstalk: –50 dB @ 1 kHz between channels.
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #   - Audible L/R bleed if gain is high.
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #✅ Minimal Circuit (if acceptable quality)
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #Left MIC  → 2.2k bias → 100nF → CD4051 I/O 0
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #Right MIC → 2.2k bias → 100nF → CD4051 I/O 1
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #Select lines GP6–GP8 (shared with pots)
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #COM out → GP26 (ADC0) already wired
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #Sample rate: **16 kHz max** to avoid MUX switching artifacts
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
10d61e39 [kimi-k2-0905] #
