10e33e8e [nitro@ryzen5] can you outline basic steps to parse, no code thanks
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #1. Grab the open-source “blendfile_reader” doc (official, C).
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #2. Read 12-byte header → identify pointer-size, endian, version.
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #3. From header, jump to first “file block”.
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #4. Walk the linked list of blocks (each has code, size, old memory address, SDNA index count).
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #5. Collect the “DNA1” block; it is a self-contained type table (structures, names, sizes,
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #alignments).
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #6. Build two lookup arrays from DNA: one for type → size/alignment, one for field → offset.
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #7. For every non-DNA block, use its code to pick the correct SDNA type entry, then stride through
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #the raw bytes with the offset table to pull any field you care about.
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #8. Ignore old memory addresses; they’re just relocation hints.
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #9. Stop when next-block pointer is zero—end of file.
10e33f72 [kimi-k2-0905] #
