10e5c8cc [nitro@ryzen5] with luma2 the chroma line can be sampled with pio
10e5c963 [kimi-k2-0905] #Yes—run the chroma pin to a comparator (or just a 74LVC gate if the swing is already 3
10e5c963 [kimi-k2-0905] #V3-compatible) and let a second PIO SM edge-count in a 280 ns window.
10e5c964 [kimi-k2-0905] #One ISR can grab the count, shift it left two bits, OR it into the same word that already holds the
10e5c964 [kimi-k2-0905] #2-bit luma value, and push the 4-bit pixel (sync-luma-chroma) to the RX FIFO.
10e5c964 [kimi-k2-0905] #Keep the chroma SM clocked at ≥ 28 MHz so one PIO cycle ≈ 35 ns; eight cycles gives you the 280 ns
10e5c965 [kimi-k2-0905] #sample window you need for C64’s colour burst phase.
10e5c965 [kimi-k2-0905] #
